> Time: 1395962205 / Thu, 27 Mar 2014 23:16:45 +0000
> URL: /admin/index.php?adsess=845f6c850772369311b67ecf8645904c&app=forums&module=forums&section=fix&st=158250
> <div style="margin:20px; margin-top:5px; "> <div class="smallfont">Quote:</div> <table cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="99%"> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border:1px inset">  Originally Posted by <strong>Tlseege</strong> <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/post/1376632"><img class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" border="0" alt="View Post"></a>  <div style="font-style:italic">bokeh is the pretty blurry background that you'll get. You get that with lower f numbers. So if you have a lens that is f1.8 you'll have beautiful blurryness... if you have f5.8, more things will be in focus and less blur.</div> </td> </tr> </table> </div>ah! i never ran across tha word before. the things you learn on bdw &lt;3<br /> <br /> and im pretty positive mid-range p&amp;s dont have lens options! but i know you can achieve that effect with a p&amp;s because ive done it on a macro setting, but its a pita and i dont have a long enough zoom for things like portraits, only works for flowers and small things like that.<br /> <br /> maria, thanks for the offer thats really sweet of you, but its going to be months before we have extra money. we have our mexico trip in 2 months and im thinking near or after christmas might be the earliest...
