array (
  'pid' => '1232368',
  'post' => '<div style="margin:20px; margin-top:5px; "> <div class="smallfont" style="margin-bottom:2px">Quote:</div> <table cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="99%"> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border:1px inset">  Originally Posted by <strong>hermosahoops</strong> <a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/post/1376503"><img class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" border="0" alt="View Post"></a>  <div style="font-style:italic">We are having a really small wedding (11 people total) and renting out a space for a reception seems excessive. Do any of you know anything about having dinner on the pier or possibly in a wine cellar?</div> </td> </tr> </table> </div>I know they can set up at the Pier, because that was my original request, but couldn\'t do it because I had too many people coming. That option though was not with the free wedding reception. That was with the silver package. I don\'t know what it would cost to have a dinner out there but I would ask. <br /> <br /> I know as a bride you get priority with the a la carte restaurants, they will make it \'semi private for you and you can reserve (usually you don\'t reserve at the a la cartes) The only drawback is that you are not allowed music there. <br /> <br /> Hope this helps.',
)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
> Time: 1395962205 / Thu, 27 Mar 2014 23:16:45 +0000
> URL: /admin/index.php?adsess=845f6c850772369311b67ecf8645904c&app=forums&module=forums&section=fix&st=158250
> <div style="margin:20px; margin-top:5px; "> <div class="smallfont">Quote:</div> <table cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="99%"> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border:1px inset">  Originally Posted by <strong>hermosahoops</strong> <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/post/1376503"><img class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" border="0" alt="View Post"></a>  <div style="font-style:italic">We are having a really small wedding (11 people total) and renting out a space for a reception seems excessive. Do any of you know anything about having dinner on the pier or possibly in a wine cellar?</div> </td> </tr> </table> </div>I know they can set up at the Pier, because that was my original request, but couldn't do it because I had too many people coming. That option though was not with the free wedding reception. That was with the silver package. I don't know what it would cost to have a dinner out there but I would ask. <br /> <br /> I know as a bride you get priority with the a la carte restaurants, they will make it 'semi private for you and you can reserve (usually you don't reserve at the a la cartes) The only drawback is that you are not allowed music there. <br /> <br /> Hope this helps.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
> Time: 1395962205 / Thu, 27 Mar 2014 23:16:45 +0000
> URL: /admin/index.php?adsess=845f6c850772369311b67ecf8645904c&app=forums&module=forums&section=fix&st=158250
> 
array (
  'pid' => '1232369',
  'post' => '<div style="margin:20px; margin-top:5px; "> <div class="smallfont" style="margin-bottom:2px">Quote:</div> <table cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="99%"> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border:1px inset">  Originally Posted by <strong>Tissey</strong> <a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/post/1376623"><img class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" border="0" alt="View Post"></a>  <div style="font-style:italic">Jacy sent me some more info. She said it was $300 to use the sound system for the reception. I\'m still thinking we may have the reception outside, but for $300 I\'m sure I can buy my own system that will be plenty loud enough.<br /> Did you get charged for delivering OOT bags? I know it say that it is a $2/room charge, but I thought I read on here that they didn\'t end up charging people for that. I asked Jacy and she told me they always charge. Bummer.</div> </td> </tr> </table> </div>Also one of the girls who went for the site visit said that the OOT bags get delivered on the guest second day because of possible room changes. I want them there when they arrive to the room. There are things in my bags that I want the guest to have immediately ie:key card holders, welcome letters. If someone changes their room they can take the bag it\'s not huge or extremely heavy. I think I will deal with the manager on that issue. As far as not charging and price differences I think it\'s just luck.....they probable forget with some.',
)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
> Time: 1395962205 / Thu, 27 Mar 2014 23:16:45 +0000
> URL: /admin/index.php?adsess=845f6c850772369311b67ecf8645904c&app=forums&module=forums&section=fix&st=158250
> <div style="margin:20px; margin-top:5px; "> <div class="smallfont">Quote:</div> <table cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="99%"> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border:1px inset">  Originally Posted by <strong>Tissey</strong> <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/post/1376623"><img class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" border="0" alt="View Post"></a>  <div style="font-style:italic">Jacy sent me some more info. She said it was $300 to use the sound system for the reception. I'm still thinking we may have the reception outside, but for $300 I'm sure I can buy my own system that will be plenty loud enough.<br /> Did you get charged for delivering OOT bags? I know it say that it is a $2/room charge, but I thought I read on here that they didn't end up charging people for that. I asked Jacy and she told me they always charge. Bummer.</div> </td> </tr> </table> </div>Also one of the girls who went for the site visit said that the OOT bags get delivered on the guest second day because of possible room changes. I want them there when they arrive to the room. There are things in my bags that I want the guest to have immediately ie:key card holders, welcome letters. If someone changes their room they can take the bag it's not huge or extremely heavy. I think I will deal with the manager on that issue. As far as not charging and price differences I think it's just luck.....they probable forget with some.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
> Time: 1395962205 / Thu, 27 Mar 2014 23:16:45 +0000
