array (
  'pid' => '1233823',
  'post' => '<br /> <br /> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>Abbie</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/thread/27891/chicks-that-click-formerly-known-as-the-photography-club-thread/2140#post_1376832"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border-bottom: 0px solid; border-left: 0px solid; border-top: 0px solid; border-right: 0px solid" /></a><br /> <br /> <div style="margin: 5px 20px 20px"> <div class="smallfont" style="margin-bottom: 2px"> Quote:</div> <table border="0" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" width="99%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border-bottom: 1px inset; border-left: 1px inset; border-top: 1px inset; border-right: 1px inset">  Originally Posted by <strong>Tlseege</strong> <a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/post/1376632"><img alt="View Post" border="0" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" /></a> <div style="font-style: italic"> bokeh is the pretty blurry background that you&#39;ll get. You get that with lower f numbers. So if you have a lens that is f1.8 you&#39;ll have beautiful blurryness... if you have f5.8, more things will be in focus and less blur.</div> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div> ah! i never ran across tha word before. the things you learn on bdw &lt;3<br /> <br /> and im pretty positive mid-range p&amp;s dont have lens options! but i know you can achieve that effect with a p&amp;s because ive done it on a macro setting, but its a pita and i dont have a long enough zoom for things like portraits, only works for flowers and small things like that.<br /> <br /> maria, thanks for the offer thats really sweet of you, but its going to be months before we have extra money. we have our mexico trip in 2 months and im thinking near or after christmas might be the earliest...</blockquote> <p> <br /> <br /> &nbsp;</p> <p> &nbsp;</p> <p> &nbsp;In macro, the depth of field&nbsp;is really tiny so you will see more blur.&nbsp; It&#39;s so tricky to get the blur with a P&amp;S, but yeah you get it sometimes.&nbsp;</p> <p> &nbsp;</p> <p> Trisha has about the best p&amp;s you&nbsp; can get (canon G11) and she was saying it&#39;s not that fast.&nbsp; Can you get the boekh with the G11?&nbsp;I really think you will need to go with an SLR to get what you want.&nbsp; You can&nbsp;get a canon rebel for around $400 (I think).&nbsp; Then buy a 50mm 1.8 lens for about $100 &amp; you can get all the blur you want.&nbsp; For sports, you&#39;ll probably want a longer lens.&nbsp;</p> <p> &nbsp;</p> <p> If you are curious about it, bokeh is a japanses word for something like pleasingly blurry.&nbsp; One camera company started using it way back &amp; it stuck.&nbsp;</p> <p> &nbsp;</p>',
)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
> Time: 1395962205 / Thu, 27 Mar 2014 23:16:45 +0000
> URL: /admin/index.php?adsess=845f6c850772369311b67ecf8645904c&app=forums&module=forums&section=fix&st=158250
> <br /> <br /> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>Abbie</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/thread/27891/chicks-that-click-formerly-known-as-the-photography-club-thread/2140#post_1376832"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border-bottom: 0px solid; border-left: 0px solid; border-top: 0px solid; border-right: 0px solid" /></a><br /> <br /> <div style="margin: 5px 20px 20px"> <div class="smallfont"> Quote:</div> <table border="0" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" width="99%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border-bottom: 1px inset; border-left: 1px inset; border-top: 1px inset; border-right: 1px inset">  Originally Posted by <strong>Tlseege</strong> <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/post/1376632"><img alt="View Post" border="0" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" /></a> <div style="font-style: italic"> bokeh is the pretty blurry background that you&#39;ll get. You get that with lower f numbers. So if you have a lens that is f1.8 you&#39;ll have beautiful blurryness... if you have f5.8, more things will be in focus and less blur.</div> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div> ah! i never ran across tha word before. the things you learn on bdw &lt;3<br /> <br /> and im pretty positive mid-range p&amp;s dont have lens options! but i know you can achieve that effect with a p&amp;s because ive done it on a macro setting, but its a pita and i dont have a long enough zoom for things like portraits, only works for flowers and small things like that.<br /> <br /> maria, thanks for the offer thats really sweet of you, but its going to be months before we have extra money. we have our mexico trip in 2 months and im thinking near or after christmas might be the earliest...</blockquote> <p> <br /> <br /> &nbsp;</p> <p> &nbsp;</p> <p> &nbsp;In macro, the depth of field&nbsp;is really tiny so you will see more blur.&nbsp; It&#39;s so tricky to get the blur with a P&amp;S, but yeah you get it sometimes.&nbsp;</p> <p> &nbsp;</p> <p> Trisha has about the best p&amp;s you&nbsp; can get (canon G11) and she was saying it&#39;s not that fast.&nbsp; Can you get the boekh with the G11?&nbsp;I really think you will need to go with an SLR to get what you want.&nbsp; You can&nbsp;get a canon rebel for around $400 (I think).&nbsp; Then buy a 50mm 1.8 lens for about $100 &amp; you can get all the blur you want.&nbsp; For sports, you&#39;ll probably want a longer lens.&nbsp;</p> <p> &nbsp;</p> <p> If you are curious about it, bokeh is a japanses word for something like pleasingly blurry.&nbsp; One camera company started using it way back &amp; it stuck.&nbsp;</p> <p> &nbsp;</p>
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
