array (
  'pid' => '1234156',
  'post' => '<p> &nbsp;</p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>dstinationdrmr</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/thread/23412/azul-sensatori-brides-post-here/9080#post_1376791"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border-right: 0px solid; border-top: 0px solid; border-left: 0px solid; border-bottom: 0px solid" /></a><br /> <div style="margin: 5px 20px 20px"> <div class="smallfont" style="margin-bottom: 2px"> Quote:</div> <table border="0" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" width="99%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border-right: 1px inset; border-top: 1px inset; border-left: 1px inset; border-bottom: 1px inset">  Originally Posted by <strong>bigboponthebeach</strong> <a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/post/1376776"><img alt="View Post" border="0" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" /></a> <div style="font-style: italic"> I too am missing Cecile!!! I am feeling spoiled because she was sooooo responsive. But I hope she si happier wherever she has gone because I&#39;m sure that can become a stressful job. :-( I just hope Faye can pull her weight and dive in working!<br /> <br /> Also, talk to a TA about what they can secure for you and take the webinar so that you can to qualify for a free room upgrade.</div> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div> Have you heard anything from Faye? I got an email from Fabio Thursday but still haven&#39;t heard from Carolina...and I&#39;m starting to freak out. I chose to procrastinate on dealing with the stuff at the resort but now that I&#39;m ready to make decisions I have had no contact with anyone to actually make plans for a month!! Kinda frustrating!!<br /> <br /> I keep asking this question, but I don&#39;t think anyone has answered me yet. How do you hear about the webinars? Is that info from your TA or the website?</blockquote> <p> I haven&#39;t heard anything from Faye yet and although I am not as close as you are with our date, I am starting to get a little flustered with the lack of communication too. I am not quite freaked out yet, but I understand your concern. I wish there was something I could say to help ease your worries here. I do think that if we are patient, it will all work out. I realize that is not saying much given your timeframe, I just get the impression that Karisma WC is REALLY understaffed right now and trying to figure out how to spread their brides out. I guess I just keep thinking that at this point, no news is good news. Is there anything you need help with right now that any of us can help you with???? You know I will help you in any way that I can, even if it means making some calls or scouring the net for you.</p> <p> &nbsp;</p> <p> I never saw you ask about the webinar, but yes....I was informed of the date and time by our very first TA. I wouldn&#39;t rely to heavily on that as a good sign though because she pushed us off in the webinar so that she could avoid answering some of the vital questions we were asking. And after the webinar still didn&#39;t do her job for her, we kicked her to the curb. I didn&#39;t think you would be interested seeing as they usually cater to the &quot;not yet booked&quot; bride and groom, but if you&#39;d like for me to ask my TA when the next one is and how to get you on it....just say the word.<br /> <br /> <span>Quote:</span></p> <div class="quote-container"> <div class="quote-block"> Originally Posted by <strong>beaz2be</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/thread/23412/azul-sensatori-brides-post-here/9090#post_1378334"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border-right: 0px solid; border-top: 0px solid; border-left: 0px solid; border-bottom: 0px solid" /></a><br /> <br /> <p> aaah!&nbsp; New Forum?!?!?!&nbsp; Changes to the look?!?!?! &nbsp;&nbsp;<img alt="" src="http://files.bestdestinationwedding.com/images/smilies/smile35.gif" title="" /> (This feels like when facebook decided to change its look all over again).&nbsp; I&#39;m a lawyer.&nbsp; We fear change.&nbsp; Sigh</p> <p> &nbsp;</p> <p> Guess it&#39;s going to take some getting used to.&nbsp; Anyone else freaked out?&nbsp; heehee.</p> <p> Hey... my pic is gone too.&nbsp; It took me FOREVER to get that in place!&nbsp;</p> <p> <img alt="" src="http://files.bestdestinationwedding.com/images/smilies/smile41.gif" title="" /></p> </div> </div> <p> I FEEL your pain here!!!! I logged on and loved the clean look but as soon as I was ready to navigate and it took me&nbsp;longer than usual, I found myself cursing and craning my neck like an old woman. I dropped a few WTF&#39;s and FI came over to see what all the hoopla was about. I am a Cop, we hate change too. LOL Letter of the law or spirit of the law....nothing in between! LOL Oh and I too hated FB&#39;s new layout. I think I have JUST come to terms with it. ;-)<br /> &nbsp;</p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>beaz2be</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/thread/23412/azul-sensatori-brides-post-here/9090#post_1378356"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border-right: 0px solid; border-top: 0px solid; border-left: 0px solid; border-bottom: 0px solid" /></a><br /> <p> Bigbop - I spoke with my TA about the upgrade to premium.&nbsp; Looks like it will cost us about 1100 or 1150 to upgrade to the premium level.&nbsp; Given that we would then &quot;save&quot; the $950 to downgrade to the Free Sweet Wedding Package, I think we&#39;ll probably go for it.&nbsp; Other than losing the bridal bouquet it seems to me like you get more with the Free Package and for just a little more we&#39;re getting the significant upgrade in accommodations.&nbsp;&nbsp; Hopefully your TA will have similar news for you.</p> <p> &nbsp;</p> <p> #2.&nbsp; I lied about my pic - it&#39;s back up on here now.</p> <p> &nbsp;</p> <p> #3.&nbsp; It won&#39;t let me delete the photo out of the quote (sorry, it&#39;s there for no reason and not related to my response to Bigbop).</p> </blockquote> <p> Yeah, this whole multi-quote thing is even going to take some getting used to!!!! GRRRRRR. I love Tammy and crew for updating things and making it prettier however the learning curve just tries my patience. :-/ I know it is for our benefit though so I digress.</p> <p> &nbsp;</p> <p> Thanks for sharing that info with me! I am still waiting on our TA to get back with us. I emailed her last Thursday to ask her to provide the costs for both classes of Suites and she has yet to respond. (That is another issue and being that she is my 2nd TA, I cannot even begin to put too much energy into that topic right now.) Anywho, as soon as I hear back from her and can do a price comparison, I will let you know how the rates fare for us. Thanks for remembering me! ;-)</p> <p> &nbsp;</p> <div class="quote-container"> <span>Quote:</span> <div class="quote-block"> Originally Posted by <strong>msmarmar123</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/thread/23412/azul-sensatori-brides-post-here/9090#post_1378631"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border-right: 0px solid; border-top: 0px solid; border-left: 0px solid; border-bottom: 0px solid" /></a><br /> <br /> <p> So...I am trying to pick colors and I think I&#39;ve decided that I really like navy blue and hot pink and white together....Has anyone used those?&nbsp; Any ideas?&nbsp; Inspirations?</p> <p> &nbsp;</p> <p> Any advice would be great :) Thanks.<br /> &nbsp;</p> </div> Ohhhhhhhhhh, let me see what I can dig up in the inspiration board department for you. I recall seeing those colors together. Hold tight, BRB..........</div>',
)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
> Time: 1395962205 / Thu, 27 Mar 2014 23:16:45 +0000
> URL: /admin/index.php?adsess=845f6c850772369311b67ecf8645904c&app=forums&module=forums&section=fix&st=158250
> <p> &nbsp;</p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>dstinationdrmr</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/thread/23412/azul-sensatori-brides-post-here/9080#post_1376791"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border-right: 0px solid; border-top: 0px solid; border-left: 0px solid; border-bottom: 0px solid" /></a><br /> <div style="margin: 5px 20px 20px"> <div class="smallfont"> Quote:</div> <table border="0" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" width="99%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border-right: 1px inset; border-top: 1px inset; border-left: 1px inset; border-bottom: 1px inset">  Originally Posted by <strong>bigboponthebeach</strong> <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/post/1376776"><img alt="View Post" border="0" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" /></a> <div style="font-style: italic"> I too am missing Cecile!!! I am feeling spoiled because she was sooooo responsive. But I hope she si happier wherever she has gone because I&#39;m sure that can become a stressful job. :-( I just hope Faye can pull her weight and dive in working!<br /> <br /> Also, talk to a TA about what they can secure for you and take the webinar so that you can to qualify for a free room upgrade.</div> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div> Have you heard anything from Faye? I got an email from Fabio Thursday but still haven&#39;t heard from Carolina...and I&#39;m starting to freak out. I chose to procrastinate on dealing with the stuff at the resort but now that I&#39;m ready to make decisions I have had no contact with anyone to actually make plans for a month!! Kinda frustrating!!<br /> <br /> I keep asking this question, but I don&#39;t think anyone has answered me yet. How do you hear about the webinars? Is that info from your TA or the website?</blockquote> <p> I haven&#39;t heard anything from Faye yet and although I am not as close as you are with our date, I am starting to get a little flustered with the lack of communication too. I am not quite freaked out yet, but I understand your concern. I wish there was something I could say to help ease your worries here. I do think that if we are patient, it will all work out. I realize that is not saying much given your timeframe, I just get the impression that Karisma WC is REALLY understaffed right now and trying to figure out how to spread their brides out. I guess I just keep thinking that at this point, no news is good news. Is there anything you need help with right now that any of us can help you with???? You know I will help you in any way that I can, even if it means making some calls or scouring the net for you.</p> <p> &nbsp;</p> <p> I never saw you ask about the webinar, but yes....I was informed of the date and time by our very first TA. I wouldn&#39;t rely to heavily on that as a good sign though because she pushed us off in the webinar so that she could avoid answering some of the vital questions we were asking. And after the webinar still didn&#39;t do her job for her, we kicked her to the curb. I didn&#39;t think you would be interested seeing as they usually cater to the &quot;not yet booked&quot; bride and groom, but if you&#39;d like for me to ask my TA when the next one is and how to get you on it....just say the word.<br /> <br /> <span>Quote:</span></p> <div class="quote-container"> <div class="quote-block"> Originally Posted by <strong>beaz2be</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/thread/23412/azul-sensatori-brides-post-here/9090#post_1378334"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border-right: 0px solid; border-top: 0px solid; border-left: 0px solid; border-bottom: 0px solid" /></a><br /> <br /> <p> aaah!&nbsp; New Forum?!?!?!&nbsp; Changes to the look?!?!?! &nbsp;&nbsp;<img alt="" src="http://files.bestdestinationwedding.com/images/smilies/smile35.gif" title="" /> (This feels like when facebook decided to change its look all over again).&nbsp; I&#39;m a lawyer.&nbsp; We fear change.&nbsp; Sigh</p> <p> &nbsp;</p> <p> Guess it&#39;s going to take some getting used to.&nbsp; Anyone else freaked out?&nbsp; heehee.</p> <p> Hey... my pic is gone too.&nbsp; It took me FOREVER to get that in place!&nbsp;</p> <p> <img alt="" src="http://files.bestdestinationwedding.com/images/smilies/smile41.gif" title="" /></p> </div> </div> <p> I FEEL your pain here!!!! I logged on and loved the clean look but as soon as I was ready to navigate and it took me&nbsp;longer than usual, I found myself cursing and craning my neck like an old woman. I dropped a few WTF&#39;s and FI came over to see what all the hoopla was about. I am a Cop, we hate change too. LOL Letter of the law or spirit of the law....nothing in between! LOL Oh and I too hated FB&#39;s new layout. I think I have JUST come to terms with it. ;-)<br /> &nbsp;</p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>beaz2be</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/thread/23412/azul-sensatori-brides-post-here/9090#post_1378356"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border-right: 0px solid; border-top: 0px solid; border-left: 0px solid; border-bottom: 0px solid" /></a><br /> <p> Bigbop - I spoke with my TA about the upgrade to premium.&nbsp; Looks like it will cost us about 1100 or 1150 to upgrade to the premium level.&nbsp; Given that we would then &quot;save&quot; the $950 to downgrade to the Free Sweet Wedding Package, I think we&#39;ll probably go for it.&nbsp; Other than losing the bridal bouquet it seems to me like you get more with the Free Package and for just a little more we&#39;re getting the significant upgrade in accommodations.&nbsp;&nbsp; Hopefully your TA will have similar news for you.</p> <p> &nbsp;</p> <p> #2.&nbsp; I lied about my pic - it&#39;s back up on here now.</p> <p> &nbsp;</p> <p> #3.&nbsp; It won&#39;t let me delete the photo out of the quote (sorry, it&#39;s there for no reason and not related to my response to Bigbop).</p> </blockquote> <p> Yeah, this whole multi-quote thing is even going to take some getting used to!!!! GRRRRRR. I love Tammy and crew for updating things and making it prettier however the learning curve just tries my patience. :-/ I know it is for our benefit though so I digress.</p> <p> &nbsp;</p> <p> Thanks for sharing that info with me! I am still waiting on our TA to get back with us. I emailed her last Thursday to ask her to provide the costs for both classes of Suites and she has yet to respond. (That is another issue and being that she is my 2nd TA, I cannot even begin to put too much energy into that topic right now.) Anywho, as soon as I hear back from her and can do a price comparison, I will let you know how the rates fare for us. Thanks for remembering me! ;-)</p> <p> &nbsp;</p> <div class="quote-container"> <span>Quote:</span> <div class="quote-block"> Originally Posted by <strong>msmarmar123</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/thread/23412/azul-sensatori-brides-post-here/9090#post_1378631"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border-right: 0px solid; border-top: 0px solid; border-left: 0px solid; border-bottom: 0px solid" /></a><br /> <br /> <p> So...I am trying to pick colors and I think I&#39;ve decided that I really like navy blue and hot pink and white together....Has anyone used those?&nbsp; Any ideas?&nbsp; Inspirations?</p> <p> &nbsp;</p> <p> Any advice would be great :) Thanks.<br /> &nbsp;</p> </div> Ohhhhhhhhhh, let me see what I can dig up in the inspiration board department for you. I recall seeing those colors together. Hold tight, BRB..........</div>
