array (
  'pid' => '1234198',
  'post' => '<p> <br /> &nbsp;</p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>KittenHeart</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/thread/23412/azul-sensatori-brides-post-here/9080#post_1376743"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border: 0px solid ;" /></a><br /> <br /> <div style="margin: 5px 20px 20px;"> <div class="smallfont" style="margin-bottom: 2px;"> Quote:</div> <table border="0" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" width="99%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border: 1px inset ;">  Originally Posted by <strong>chong</strong> <a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/post/1376645"><img alt="View Post" border="0" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" /></a> <div style="font-style: italic;"> I am not having any flowers on my wedding ceremony area - except for the two hanging flowers and rose pedals that comes with the exotic gazebo package. I figure that is enough for 15 min ceremony site :)</div> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div> That&#39;s all I had, I requested all white flowers and natural greens for the hanging flowers on the chuppah thing on the Sky Deck and white rose petals down the aisle and it was gorgeous. I think we have similar tastes :)<br /> <br /> Also, the reception seating is best figured out on site. I struggled with this for weeks and Kiara even made me seating chart options to give me a better idea BUT she also told me I had to have square tables and when I got there, they told me they would be round tables... which I preferred anyways so it worked out for the best.</blockquote> <p> <br /> I did send our &quot;vision&quot; on what we thought was the best table setup. I hope we can get what we want... but until I really see the area for myself, I am not sure about our table setup. Thanks for the info!<br /> <br /> &nbsp;</p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>beaz2be</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/thread/23412/azul-sensatori-brides-post-here/9090#post_1378334"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border: 0px solid ;" /></a><br /> <br /> <p> aaah!&nbsp; New Forum?!?!?!&nbsp; Changes to the look?!?!?! &nbsp;&nbsp;<img alt="" src="http://files.bestdestinationwedding.com/images/smilies/smile35.gif" title="" /> (This feels like when facebook decided to change its look all over again).&nbsp; I&#39;m a lawyer.&nbsp; We fear change.&nbsp; Sigh</p> <p> &nbsp;</p> <p> Guess it&#39;s going to take some getting used to.&nbsp; Anyone else freaked out?&nbsp; heehee.</p> <p> Hey... my pic is gone too.&nbsp; It took me FOREVER to get that in place!&nbsp;</p> <p> <img alt="" src="http://files.bestdestinationwedding.com/images/smilies/smile41.gif" title="" /></p> </blockquote> <p> <br /> <br /> I don&#39;t like it. I hate changes and I thought I log onto a wrong forum at first. I don&#39;t have the wedding day countdown ticker...where is go? and now I cannot tell when people are getting married... <img alt="" src="http://files.bestdestinationwedding.com/images/smilies/smile105.gif" title="" /><br /> &nbsp;</p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>msmarmar123</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/thread/23412/azul-sensatori-brides-post-here/9090#post_1378631"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border: 0px solid ;" /></a><br /> <br /> <p> So...I am trying to pick colors and I think I&#39;ve decided that I really like navy blue and hot pink and white together....Has anyone used those?&nbsp; Any ideas?&nbsp; Inspirations?</p> <p> &nbsp;</p> <p> Any advice would be great :) Thanx</p> </blockquote> <p> <br /> I have blue and pink together! My bridesmaids dress color is blue and all the flowers are pink and white. I don&#39;t have any inspiration board together (I am too lazy). I have attached my bouquet picture that I want - pink &amp; white combo. I am not sure if this picture will show. I am not sure how to attach pictures any more <img alt="" src="http://files.bestdestinationwedding.com/images/smilies/cry.gif" title="" /></p> <p> &nbsp;</p> <p> &nbsp;</p> <span huddler_attributes="{&quot;plugin&quot;:&quot;attachment&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;7394&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Bouquet.jpg&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;size&quot;:&quot;72&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;jpg&quot;}}" huddler_plugin="attachment">&nbsp;</span> <p> &nbsp;</p>',
)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
> Time: 1395962205 / Thu, 27 Mar 2014 23:16:45 +0000
> URL: /admin/index.php?adsess=845f6c850772369311b67ecf8645904c&app=forums&module=forums&section=fix&st=158250
> <p> <br /> &nbsp;</p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>KittenHeart</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/thread/23412/azul-sensatori-brides-post-here/9080#post_1376743"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border: 0px solid ;" /></a><br /> <br /> <div style="margin: 5px 20px 20px;"> <div class="smallfont"> Quote:</div> <table border="0" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" width="99%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border: 1px inset ;">  Originally Posted by <strong>chong</strong> <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/post/1376645"><img alt="View Post" border="0" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" /></a> <div style="font-style: italic;"> I am not having any flowers on my wedding ceremony area - except for the two hanging flowers and rose pedals that comes with the exotic gazebo package. I figure that is enough for 15 min ceremony site :)</div> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div> That&#39;s all I had, I requested all white flowers and natural greens for the hanging flowers on the chuppah thing on the Sky Deck and white rose petals down the aisle and it was gorgeous. I think we have similar tastes :)<br /> <br /> Also, the reception seating is best figured out on site. I struggled with this for weeks and Kiara even made me seating chart options to give me a better idea BUT she also told me I had to have square tables and when I got there, they told me they would be round tables... which I preferred anyways so it worked out for the best.</blockquote> <p> <br /> I did send our &quot;vision&quot; on what we thought was the best table setup. I hope we can get what we want... but until I really see the area for myself, I am not sure about our table setup. Thanks for the info!<br /> <br /> &nbsp;</p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>beaz2be</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/thread/23412/azul-sensatori-brides-post-here/9090#post_1378334"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border: 0px solid ;" /></a><br /> <br /> <p> aaah!&nbsp; New Forum?!?!?!&nbsp; Changes to the look?!?!?! &nbsp;&nbsp;<img alt="" src="http://files.bestdestinationwedding.com/images/smilies/smile35.gif" title="" /> (This feels like when facebook decided to change its look all over again).&nbsp; I&#39;m a lawyer.&nbsp; We fear change.&nbsp; Sigh</p> <p> &nbsp;</p> <p> Guess it&#39;s going to take some getting used to.&nbsp; Anyone else freaked out?&nbsp; heehee.</p> <p> Hey... my pic is gone too.&nbsp; It took me FOREVER to get that in place!&nbsp;</p> <p> <img alt="" src="http://files.bestdestinationwedding.com/images/smilies/smile41.gif" title="" /></p> </blockquote> <p> <br /> <br /> I don&#39;t like it. I hate changes and I thought I log onto a wrong forum at first. I don&#39;t have the wedding day countdown ticker...where is go? and now I cannot tell when people are getting married... <img alt="" src="http://files.bestdestinationwedding.com/images/smilies/smile105.gif" title="" /><br /> &nbsp;</p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>msmarmar123</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/thread/23412/azul-sensatori-brides-post-here/9090#post_1378631"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border: 0px solid ;" /></a><br /> <br /> <p> So...I am trying to pick colors and I think I&#39;ve decided that I really like navy blue and hot pink and white together....Has anyone used those?&nbsp; Any ideas?&nbsp; Inspirations?</p> <p> &nbsp;</p> <p> Any advice would be great :) Thanx</p> </blockquote> <p> <br /> I have blue and pink together! My bridesmaids dress color is blue and all the flowers are pink and white. I don&#39;t have any inspiration board together (I am too lazy). I have attached my bouquet picture that I want - pink &amp; white combo. I am not sure if this picture will show. I am not sure how to attach pictures any more <img alt="" src="http://files.bestdestinationwedding.com/images/smilies/cry.gif" title="" /></p> <p> &nbsp;</p> <p> &nbsp;</p> <span huddler_attributes="{&quot;plugin&quot;:&quot;attachment&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;7394&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Bouquet.jpg&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;size&quot;:&quot;72&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;jpg&quot;}}" huddler_plugin="attachment">&nbsp;</span> <p> &nbsp;</p>
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
