> Time: 1395962205 / Thu, 27 Mar 2014 23:16:45 +0000
> URL: /admin/index.php?adsess=845f6c850772369311b67ecf8645904c&app=forums&module=forums&section=fix&st=158250
> 
array (
  'pid' => '1234272',
  'post' => '<p> THANKS for all of the feedback ladies!<br /> &nbsp;</p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>murmel</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/thread/23412/azul-sensatori-brides-post-here/9080#post_1376647"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border: 0px solid;" /></a><br /> <br /> [QUOTE=amandamarieb;1376148]Ok Ladies so I need som help deciding on flowers. i thought that I send you photos of my &quot;look&quot; so you can have a good idea of what else is going on.<br /> <br /> I want to have dried lilac running the aisles: <a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="http://vickysgarden.com/images/site/driedLilacs.jpg"><img alt="Click the image to open in full size." border="0" class="tcattdimgresizer" src="http://vickysgarden.com/images/site/driedLilacs.jpg" /></a><br /> <br /> I was originally going to do all white and green flowers but now think that there needs to be some more color. What do you think?<br /> <br /> To go along with the ones I&#39;ve shown you, which do you think would work best given my adversion to too much color and wanting everything to feel antiquey and romantic?<br /> <br /> [QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Love the dress! The suits for the men looks lovely and will go great with the girls sage dresses.<br /> <br /> As for the flowers...if you are going with the antique feel, I would go with the muted tones. Maybe add a touch of the lilacs to your bouquet to tie in with the decor.<br /> <br /> Also a warm welcome to Lauren and Gemma! :)</blockquote> <p> <br /> <br /> <br /> &nbsp;</p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>KittenHeart</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/thread/23412/azul-sensatori-brides-post-here/9080#post_1376743"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border: 0px solid;" /></a><br /> <br /> <div style="margin:20px; margin-top:5px; "> <div class="smallfont" style="margin-bottom:2px"> Quote:</div> <table border="0" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" width="99%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border:1px inset">  Originally Posted by <strong>chong</strong> <a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/post/1376645"><img alt="View Post" border="0" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" /></a> <div style="font-style:italic"> I am not having any flowers on my wedding ceremony area - except for the two hanging flowers and rose pedals that comes with the exotic gazebo package. I figure that is enough for 15 min ceremony site :)</div> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div> That&#39;s all I had, I requested all white flowers and natural greens for the hanging flowers on the chuppah thing on the Sky Deck and white rose petals down the aisle and it was gorgeous. I think we have similar tastes :)<br /> <br /> Also, the reception seating is best figured out on site. I struggled with this for weeks and Kiara even made me seating chart options to give me a better idea BUT she also told me I had to have square tables and when I got there, they told me they would be round tables... which I preferred anyways so it worked out for the best.</blockquote> <p> That stinks. I am really concerned about the seating chart because we will have about 70 guests and many won&#39;t know one another. I want people to feel comfortable so I wanted to assign them at tables with people that they know. I suppose they do hav a few days to make friends though.&nbsp;</p> <p> &nbsp;</p> <p> Did you have table cards? I am using photo frames with place cards as we are doing a make-shift photo booth section and the frames will fit the photos, hence place cards and favors in one. :) Maybe I can just each table member&#39;s photo frame with placard lined up together and I can put a table number flat on the table in front of that row. Wow, I hope that makes sense when you read it. For a professional communicator sometimes I have real issues. :)<br /> <br /> <br /> &nbsp;</p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>amybermuda</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/thread/23412/azul-sensatori-brides-post-here/9090#post_1376941"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border: 0px solid;" /></a><br /> <br /> <div style="margin:20px; margin-top:5px; "> <div class="smallfont" style="margin-bottom:2px"> &nbsp;</blockquote> <br /> <div style="margin:20px; margin-top:5px; "> <div class="smallfont" style="margin-bottom:2px"> Quote:</div> <table border="0" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" width="99%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border:1px inset">  Originally Posted by <strong>amandamarieb</strong> <a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/post/1376148"><img alt="View Post" border="0" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" /></a> <div style="font-style:italic"> Ok Ladies so I need som help deciding on flowers. i thought that I send you photos of my &quot;look&quot; so you can have a good idea of what else is going on.<br /> <br /> They are also wearing matching vests and sage green ties<br /> <br /> Here are the bridesmaids dresses:<br /> <br /> They will be in sage green incase that didnt show up<br /> <br /> I am going to have 6 of these bouquets tied to chivalir chairs with gold bows. They will line the aisles as well:<br /> <br /> I want to have dried lilac running the aisles<br /> <br /> I was originally going to do all white and green flowers but now think that there needs to be some more color. What do you think?<br /> <br /> To go along with the ones I&#39;ve shown you, which do you think would work best given my adversion to too much color and wanting everything to feel antiquey and romantic?<br /> <br /> Here&#39;s one option. I would change a couple of thinsg...no branches out of the top and a gold ribbon. Also more garden green filler instead of bright green.<br /> <br /> Let me know what you think.Thanks for the input ladies!<br /> Purple Summer Wedding Flowers Photo by Floral Verde LLC | WeddingWire<br /> <br /> Again, no random twigs sticking out if I go with these and also less bright green filler, more garden green. And a gold ribbon tying them all together. :)</div> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div> I love the gold ribbon! Everything is going to be gorgeous Amanda. I love your theme/feel of your wedding. Its going to be so romantic... Kind of like a MidSummer Nights Dream kind of feel. My sister had a wedding like that and it was amazing. Just thinking about it makes me feel all warm and lovey.<br /> <br /> I like the Wedding wire bouquet best. I think just a small hint of purple here and there as an accent will really bring out the green you have chosen. And honestly I don&#39;t think green and white needs much accent.<br /> <br /> Are you going to do seating cards (I forget their formal name)? I think gold calligraphy hand written names would look really nice and go with your theme.<br /> <br /> <div style="margin:20px; margin-top:5px; "> <div class="smallfont" style="margin-bottom:2px"> Quote:</div> <table border="0" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" width="99%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border:1px inset">  Originally Posted by <strong>amandamarieb</strong> <a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/post/1376273"><img alt="View Post" border="0" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" /></a> <div style="font-style:italic"> Take my advice and look into every promotion the other girls on this thread mention getting. That&#39;s what I did and now I have saved myself well over 3k.</div> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div> That&#39;s wicked! They are offering so much better rates and packages and little deals than when I booked. You really made out like a bandit!!!</div> </div> <p> THANKS so much! You think that the green and white will work? Ah, that makes me feel better. Maybe the lilac running the aisles will be enough. And maybe I can request a touch of purple in my bouquet and BM&#39;s can have the all white and green. I guess I&#39;ll have to wait and see what the quoted Lomas comes back with are like. I wish I felt comfortable sending them pictures of two bouquets and saying, &quot;merge these&quot; or saying &quot;can you add a hint of purple&quot; to the white and green bouquet but I am scared of what I will see when I get them. Honestly, I know that the flowers are going to look spectacular because all of yours did (better than the photos you sent to Lomas actually) but I am bit of a control freak. Not that I need to have an exact thing but there are some things that I just don&#39;t want. I am fearful that&#39;s exactly what I will get. So I figure better to furnish them with photos and asking them to duplicate.&nbsp;</p> <p> &nbsp;</p> <p> Anyway, I let you ladies know what I decide when I get the quotes. I can&#39;t thank you enough for the help.&nbsp;<br /> <br /> <br /> &nbsp;</p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>beaz2be</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/thread/23412/azul-sensatori-brides-post-here/9090#post_1378334"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border: 0px solid;" /></a><br /> <br /> <p> aaah!&nbsp; New Forum?!?!?!&nbsp; Changes to the look?!?!?! &nbsp;&nbsp;<img alt="" src="http://files.bestdestinationwedding.com/images/smilies/smile35.gif" title="" /> (This feels like when facebook decided to change its look all over again).&nbsp; I&#39;m a lawyer.&nbsp; We fear change.&nbsp; Sigh</p> <p> &nbsp;</p> <p> Guess it&#39;s going to take some getting used to.&nbsp; Anyone else freaked out?&nbsp; heehee.</p> <p> Hey... my pic is gone too.&nbsp; It took me FOREVER to get that in place!&nbsp;</p> <p> <img alt="" src="http://files.bestdestinationwedding.com/images/smilies/smile41.gif" title="" /></p> </blockquote> <p> I know. I am sure it is like 1 million times better I am just getting down to crunch time and hate to have to learn it all over again. I am just so glad that it&#39;s back. I freaked out earlier today when I saw that it was being redone. I really assumed it was going to be down for a week or so. They ladies did a great job getting it done so quickly. &nbsp;<br /> <br /> <br /> &nbsp;</p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>MaggieandJay</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/thread/23412/azul-sensatori-brides-post-here/9090#post_1378697"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border: 0px solid;" /></a><br /> <br /> <p> Ok ladies! Round one of the logos are in! Let me know what you think!</p> <p> &nbsp;</p> <p> &nbsp;</p> <span huddler_attributes="{&quot;plugin&quot;:&quot;attachment&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;7393&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Monograms Version 1.pdf&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Possible Monograms for my wedding&quot;,&quot;size&quot;:&quot;198&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;pdf&quot;}}" huddler_plugin="attachment">&nbsp;</span> <p> &nbsp;</p> </blockquote> <p> <br /> I can&#39;t open. :( It says &quot;system error&quot;<br /> <br /> &nbsp;</p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>chong</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/thread/23412/azul-sensatori-brides-post-here/9100#post_1378710"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border: 0px solid;" /></a><br /> <br /> <p> So I am about to order my FREE brochures from VISTAPRINT... I am finding out that it&#39;s not really FREE. I have to pay for $5 per picture download and shipping is like $11 for standard shipping. I guess overall it&#39;s cheaper but didn&#39;t realized that it will cost me about the money I am saving from the FREE promotion. Is this typical?</p> </blockquote> <p> <br /> That stinks...but usually not the case. I have ordered a few things through them and the promotions have ben pretty true. You&#39;ll always have to pay for shipping thought.&nbsp;<br /> <br /> &nbsp;</p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>bigboponthebeach</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/thread/23412/azul-sensatori-brides-post-here/9100#post_1378760"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border: 0px solid;" /></a><br /> <br /> <p> <span>Quote:</span></p> <p> <br /> Hey Maggie! I tried to look at these and I got a &quot;System Error.&quot; After giving it three tries, I had no luck. Maybe you can do the photbucket thingy if others cannot see them as well? I think this has something to do with the new format because I&#39;ve never run into an issue like that before trying to open a pdf. attachment here. <img alt="" height="16" src="http://files.bestdestinationwedding.com/images/smilies/huh.gif" title="" width="16" /><br /> &nbsp;</p> </blockquote> <p> <br /> Me too. Bummer.&nbsp;<br /> <br /> &nbsp;</p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>bigboponthebeach</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/thread/23412/azul-sensatori-brides-post-here/9100#post_1378762"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border: 0px solid;" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <p> <br /> I too don&#39;t like that the ticker is gone. That was one of the ways that I kept track of who was who as well when usernames&#39;s failed my memory. I&#39;m sure they will work that kink out though in due time because everybody loves their ticker&#39;s, even the moderators who have been married for years and are now counting down their second or third pregnancy. LOL</p> <p> &nbsp;</p> <p> Your bouquet choice is beautiful and I like the pink speckles in the white flower. What is that type of flower called? I&#39;ve seen a fire and ice rose that looks similar, but never one that has that tropical look. Pretty!<br /> &nbsp;</p> </blockquote> <p> I KNOW!!! So sad. I still don&#39;t have a profile pic. The ticker was all that I had. Now I will have to look at theknot.com to find out how many days until my wedding. Since I found this forum, I haven&#39;t really used that site. This one is so much more helpful thanks to all of you.&nbsp;<br /> &nbsp;</p>',
)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
> Time: 1395962205 / Thu, 27 Mar 2014 23:16:45 +0000
> URL: /admin/index.php?adsess=845f6c850772369311b67ecf8645904c&app=forums&module=forums&section=fix&st=158250
> <p> THANKS for all of the feedback ladies!<br /> &nbsp;</p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>murmel</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/thread/23412/azul-sensatori-brides-post-here/9080#post_1376647"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border: 0px solid;" /></a><br /> <br /> [QUOTE=amandamarieb;1376148]Ok Ladies so I need som help deciding on flowers. i thought that I send you photos of my &quot;look&quot; so you can have a good idea of what else is going on.<br /> <br /> I want to have dried lilac running the aisles: <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="http://vickysgarden.com/images/site/driedLilacs.jpg"><img alt="Click the image to open in full size." border="0" class="tcattdimgresizer" src="http://vickysgarden.com/images/site/driedLilacs.jpg" /></a><br /> <br /> I was originally going to do all white and green flowers but now think that there needs to be some more color. What do you think?<br /> <br /> To go along with the ones I&#39;ve shown you, which do you think would work best given my adversion to too much color and wanting everything to feel antiquey and romantic?<br /> <br /> [QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Love the dress! The suits for the men looks lovely and will go great with the girls sage dresses.<br /> <br /> As for the flowers...if you are going with the antique feel, I would go with the muted tones. Maybe add a touch of the lilacs to your bouquet to tie in with the decor.<br /> <br /> Also a warm welcome to Lauren and Gemma! :)</blockquote> <p> <br /> <br /> <br /> &nbsp;</p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>KittenHeart</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/thread/23412/azul-sensatori-brides-post-here/9080#post_1376743"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border: 0px solid;" /></a><br /> <br /> <div style="margin:20px; margin-top:5px; "> <div class="smallfont"> Quote:</div> <table border="0" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" width="99%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border:1px inset">  Originally Posted by <strong>chong</strong> <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/post/1376645"><img alt="View Post" border="0" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" /></a> <div style="font-style:italic"> I am not having any flowers on my wedding ceremony area - except for the two hanging flowers and rose pedals that comes with the exotic gazebo package. I figure that is enough for 15 min ceremony site :)</div> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div> That&#39;s all I had, I requested all white flowers and natural greens for the hanging flowers on the chuppah thing on the Sky Deck and white rose petals down the aisle and it was gorgeous. I think we have similar tastes :)<br /> <br /> Also, the reception seating is best figured out on site. I struggled with this for weeks and Kiara even made me seating chart options to give me a better idea BUT she also told me I had to have square tables and when I got there, they told me they would be round tables... which I preferred anyways so it worked out for the best.</blockquote> <p> That stinks. I am really concerned about the seating chart because we will have about 70 guests and many won&#39;t know one another. I want people to feel comfortable so I wanted to assign them at tables with people that they know. I suppose they do hav a few days to make friends though.&nbsp;</p> <p> &nbsp;</p> <p> Did you have table cards? I am using photo frames with place cards as we are doing a make-shift photo booth section and the frames will fit the photos, hence place cards and favors in one. :) Maybe I can just each table member&#39;s photo frame with placard lined up together and I can put a table number flat on the table in front of that row. Wow, I hope that makes sense when you read it. For a professional communicator sometimes I have real issues. :)<br /> <br /> <br /> &nbsp;</p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>amybermuda</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/thread/23412/azul-sensatori-brides-post-here/9090#post_1376941"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border: 0px solid;" /></a><br /> <br /> <div style="margin:20px; margin-top:5px; "> <div class="smallfont"> &nbsp;</blockquote> <br /> <div style="margin:20px; margin-top:5px; "> <div class="smallfont"> Quote:</div> <table border="0" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" width="99%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border:1px inset">  Originally Posted by <strong>amandamarieb</strong> <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/post/1376148"><img alt="View Post" border="0" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" /></a> <div style="font-style:italic"> Ok Ladies so I need som help deciding on flowers. i thought that I send you photos of my &quot;look&quot; so you can have a good idea of what else is going on.<br /> <br /> They are also wearing matching vests and sage green ties<br /> <br /> Here are the bridesmaids dresses:<br /> <br /> They will be in sage green incase that didnt show up<br /> <br /> I am going to have 6 of these bouquets tied to chivalir chairs with gold bows. They will line the aisles as well:<br /> <br /> I want to have dried lilac running the aisles<br /> <br /> I was originally going to do all white and green flowers but now think that there needs to be some more color. What do you think?<br /> <br /> To go along with the ones I&#39;ve shown you, which do you think would work best given my adversion to too much color and wanting everything to feel antiquey and romantic?<br /> <br /> Here&#39;s one option. I would change a couple of thinsg...no branches out of the top and a gold ribbon. Also more garden green filler instead of bright green.<br /> <br /> Let me know what you think.Thanks for the input ladies!<br /> Purple Summer Wedding Flowers Photo by Floral Verde LLC | WeddingWire<br /> <br /> Again, no random twigs sticking out if I go with these and also less bright green filler, more garden green. And a gold ribbon tying them all together. :)</div> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div> I love the gold ribbon! Everything is going to be gorgeous Amanda. I love your theme/feel of your wedding. Its going to be so romantic... Kind of like a MidSummer Nights Dream kind of feel. My sister had a wedding like that and it was amazing. Just thinking about it makes me feel all warm and lovey.<br /> <br /> I like the Wedding wire bouquet best. I think just a small hint of purple here and there as an accent will really bring out the green you have chosen. And honestly I don&#39;t think green and white needs much accent.<br /> <br /> Are you going to do seating cards (I forget their formal name)? I think gold calligraphy hand written names would look really nice and go with your theme.<br /> <br /> <div style="margin:20px; margin-top:5px; "> <div class="smallfont"> Quote:</div> <table border="0" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" width="99%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border:1px inset">  Originally Posted by <strong>amandamarieb</strong> <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/post/1376273"><img alt="View Post" border="0" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" /></a> <div style="font-style:italic"> Take my advice and look into every promotion the other girls on this thread mention getting. That&#39;s what I did and now I have saved myself well over 3k.</div> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div> That&#39;s wicked! They are offering so much better rates and packages and little deals than when I booked. You really made out like a bandit!!!</div> </div> <p> THANKS so much! You think that the green and white will work? Ah, that makes me feel better. Maybe the lilac running the aisles will be enough. And maybe I can request a touch of purple in my bouquet and BM&#39;s can have the all white and green. I guess I&#39;ll have to wait and see what the quoted Lomas comes back with are like. I wish I felt comfortable sending them pictures of two bouquets and saying, &quot;merge these&quot; or saying &quot;can you add a hint of purple&quot; to the white and green bouquet but I am scared of what I will see when I get them. Honestly, I know that the flowers are going to look spectacular because all of yours did (better than the photos you sent to Lomas actually) but I am bit of a control freak. Not that I need to have an exact thing but there are some things that I just don&#39;t want. I am fearful that&#39;s exactly what I will get. So I figure better to furnish them with photos and asking them to duplicate.&nbsp;</p> <p> &nbsp;</p> <p> Anyway, I let you ladies know what I decide when I get the quotes. I can&#39;t thank you enough for the help.&nbsp;<br /> <br /> <br /> &nbsp;</p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>beaz2be</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/thread/23412/azul-sensatori-brides-post-here/9090#post_1378334"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border: 0px solid;" /></a><br /> <br /> <p> aaah!&nbsp; New Forum?!?!?!&nbsp; Changes to the look?!?!?! &nbsp;&nbsp;<img alt="" src="http://files.bestdestinationwedding.com/images/smilies/smile35.gif" title="" /> (This feels like when facebook decided to change its look all over again).&nbsp; I&#39;m a lawyer.&nbsp; We fear change.&nbsp; Sigh</p> <p> &nbsp;</p> <p> Guess it&#39;s going to take some getting used to.&nbsp; Anyone else freaked out?&nbsp; heehee.</p> <p> Hey... my pic is gone too.&nbsp; It took me FOREVER to get that in place!&nbsp;</p> <p> <img alt="" src="http://files.bestdestinationwedding.com/images/smilies/smile41.gif" title="" /></p> </blockquote> <p> I know. I am sure it is like 1 million times better I am just getting down to crunch time and hate to have to learn it all over again. I am just so glad that it&#39;s back. I freaked out earlier today when I saw that it was being redone. I really assumed it was going to be down for a week or so. They ladies did a great job getting it done so quickly. &nbsp;<br /> <br /> <br /> &nbsp;</p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>MaggieandJay</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/thread/23412/azul-sensatori-brides-post-here/9090#post_1378697"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border: 0px solid;" /></a><br /> <br /> <p> Ok ladies! Round one of the logos are in! Let me know what you think!</p> <p> &nbsp;</p> <p> &nbsp;</p> <span huddler_attributes="{&quot;plugin&quot;:&quot;attachment&quot;,&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;7393&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Monograms Version 1.pdf&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Possible Monograms for my wedding&quot;,&quot;size&quot;:&quot;198&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;pdf&quot;}}" huddler_plugin="attachment">&nbsp;</span> <p> &nbsp;</p> </blockquote> <p> <br /> I can&#39;t open. :( It says &quot;system error&quot;<br /> <br /> &nbsp;</p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>chong</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/thread/23412/azul-sensatori-brides-post-here/9100#post_1378710"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border: 0px solid;" /></a><br /> <br /> <p> So I am about to order my FREE brochures from VISTAPRINT... I am finding out that it&#39;s not really FREE. I have to pay for $5 per picture download and shipping is like $11 for standard shipping. I guess overall it&#39;s cheaper but didn&#39;t realized that it will cost me about the money I am saving from the FREE promotion. Is this typical?</p> </blockquote> <p> <br /> That stinks...but usually not the case. I have ordered a few things through them and the promotions have ben pretty true. You&#39;ll always have to pay for shipping thought.&nbsp;<br /> <br /> &nbsp;</p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>bigboponthebeach</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/thread/23412/azul-sensatori-brides-post-here/9100#post_1378760"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border: 0px solid;" /></a><br /> <br /> <p> <span>Quote:</span></p> <p> <br /> Hey Maggie! I tried to look at these and I got a &quot;System Error.&quot; After giving it three tries, I had no luck. Maybe you can do the photbucket thingy if others cannot see them as well? I think this has something to do with the new format because I&#39;ve never run into an issue like that before trying to open a pdf. attachment here. <img alt="" height="16" src="http://files.bestdestinationwedding.com/images/smilies/huh.gif" title="" width="16" /><br /> &nbsp;</p> </blockquote> <p> <br /> Me too. Bummer.&nbsp;<br /> <br /> &nbsp;</p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>bigboponthebeach</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/thread/23412/azul-sensatori-brides-post-here/9100#post_1378762"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border: 0px solid;" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <p> <br /> I too don&#39;t like that the ticker is gone. That was one of the ways that I kept track of who was who as well when usernames&#39;s failed my memory. I&#39;m sure they will work that kink out though in due time because everybody loves their ticker&#39;s, even the moderators who have been married for years and are now counting down their second or third pregnancy. LOL</p> <p> &nbsp;</p> <p> Your bouquet choice is beautiful and I like the pink speckles in the white flower. What is that type of flower called? I&#39;ve seen a fire and ice rose that looks similar, but never one that has that tropical look. Pretty!<br /> &nbsp;</p> </blockquote> <p> I KNOW!!! So sad. I still don&#39;t have a profile pic. The ticker was all that I had. Now I will have to look at theknot.com to find out how many days until my wedding. Since I found this forum, I haven&#39;t really used that site. This one is so much more helpful thanks to all of you.&nbsp;<br /> &nbsp;</p>
