array (
  'pid' => '1235122',
  'post' => '<p> <br /> <br /> &nbsp;</p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>murmel</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/thread/55989/dress-is-in-and-its-not-good#post_1376682"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border-right: 0px solid; border-top: 0px solid; border-left: 0px solid; border-bottom: 0px solid" /></a><br /> <br /> <div style="margin: 5px 20px 20px"> <div class="smallfont" style="margin-bottom: 2px"> Quote:</div> <table border="0" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" width="99%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border-right: 1px inset; border-top: 1px inset; border-left: 1px inset; border-bottom: 1px inset">  Originally Posted by <strong>CanadianLindsey</strong> <a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/post/1376220"><img alt="View Post" border="0" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" /></a> <div style="font-style: italic"> The same thing is happening to me. I was the last appt during a trunk show and I guess the saleswoman was distracted because when my real dress came in and I tried it on it was huge on me-2 sizes too big! To be honest in all of the excitement I didn&#39;t even look at what size she measured me at and what size she actually ordered. Now I am thinking I should ask the store to give me a deal on alterations b/c of the mistake, but I have heard their seamstress is expensive and hard to deal with since no one speaks english there! It does ruin the moment a bit when you put on &quot;your dress&quot; and it doesn&#39;t fit...at all! But hopefully we will all end up happy once it fits. Fingers crossed.............</div> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div> Where are you in Canada? If you&#39;re in the Toronto area I have a wonderful seamstress and is pretty reasonable pricewise. Good luck!</blockquote> <p> <br /> Thank you for the&nbsp;offer and encouragement!&nbsp; I am in Alberta though, but I did call the bridal store on Monday and made an appointment to try the dress on while the stores owner is in.&nbsp; So hopefully she will see that it is their measurement error and do the alterations at a discount.&nbsp; Otherwise, I&#39;m taking my dress and my money elsewhere!!<br /> &nbsp;</p>',
)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
> Time: 1395962205 / Thu, 27 Mar 2014 23:16:45 +0000
> URL: /admin/index.php?adsess=845f6c850772369311b67ecf8645904c&app=forums&module=forums&section=fix&st=158250
> <p> <br /> <br /> &nbsp;</p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>murmel</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/thread/55989/dress-is-in-and-its-not-good#post_1376682"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border-right: 0px solid; border-top: 0px solid; border-left: 0px solid; border-bottom: 0px solid" /></a><br /> <br /> <div style="margin: 5px 20px 20px"> <div class="smallfont"> Quote:</div> <table border="0" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" width="99%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border-right: 1px inset; border-top: 1px inset; border-left: 1px inset; border-bottom: 1px inset">  Originally Posted by <strong>CanadianLindsey</strong> <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/post/1376220"><img alt="View Post" border="0" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" /></a> <div style="font-style: italic"> The same thing is happening to me. I was the last appt during a trunk show and I guess the saleswoman was distracted because when my real dress came in and I tried it on it was huge on me-2 sizes too big! To be honest in all of the excitement I didn&#39;t even look at what size she measured me at and what size she actually ordered. Now I am thinking I should ask the store to give me a deal on alterations b/c of the mistake, but I have heard their seamstress is expensive and hard to deal with since no one speaks english there! It does ruin the moment a bit when you put on &quot;your dress&quot; and it doesn&#39;t fit...at all! But hopefully we will all end up happy once it fits. Fingers crossed.............</div> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div> Where are you in Canada? If you&#39;re in the Toronto area I have a wonderful seamstress and is pretty reasonable pricewise. Good luck!</blockquote> <p> <br /> Thank you for the&nbsp;offer and encouragement!&nbsp; I am in Alberta though, but I did call the bridal store on Monday and made an appointment to try the dress on while the stores owner is in.&nbsp; So hopefully she will see that it is their measurement error and do the alterations at a discount.&nbsp; Otherwise, I&#39;m taking my dress and my money elsewhere!!<br /> &nbsp;</p>
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
