array (
  'pid' => '1249821',
  'post' => '<p> <br /> <br /> &nbsp;</p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>Sunandsand</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/thread/61783/sunandsand-s-dreams-la-romana-wedding-review-a-dream/10#post_1372320"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border-right: 0px solid; border-top: 0px solid; border-left: 0px solid; border-bottom: 0px solid" /></a><br /> <br /> <div style="margin: 5px 20px 20px"> <div class="smallfont" style="margin-bottom: 2px"> Quote:</div> <table border="0" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" width="99%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border-right: 1px inset; border-top: 1px inset; border-left: 1px inset; border-bottom: 1px inset">  Originally Posted by <strong>ReeRee</strong> <a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/post/1371536"><img alt="View Post" border="0" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" /></a> <div style="font-style: italic"> You two look wonderful in those beautiful pics!! Question, where did your husband get his white shirts and slacks from?? I want my FI to have similar all white attire as well.</div> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div> Hey ReeRee,<br /> The shirt was Banana Republic and the pants were from Tristan (Canadian company). We saw similar ones at Armani Exchange.<br /> <br /> It&#39;s funny because his mom was so upset he was not going to be wearing a suit. She called us every day leading up to the wedding to get him to change his mind. After a while, he started shopping for blazers to appease her and I had to remind him that this original outfit is what he wanted. He looked great PLUS he would have been miserable with more clothes on in that heat.</blockquote> <p> <br /> Thank you Sunandsand! It gives me great idea where to shop for my FI!&nbsp; And I understand how in-laws can be sometimes;)<br /> &nbsp;</p>',
)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
> Time: 1395962205 / Thu, 27 Mar 2014 23:16:45 +0000
> URL: /admin/index.php?adsess=845f6c850772369311b67ecf8645904c&app=forums&module=forums&section=fix&st=158250
> <p> <br /> <br /> &nbsp;</p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>Sunandsand</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/thread/61783/sunandsand-s-dreams-la-romana-wedding-review-a-dream/10#post_1372320"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border-right: 0px solid; border-top: 0px solid; border-left: 0px solid; border-bottom: 0px solid" /></a><br /> <br /> <div style="margin: 5px 20px 20px"> <div class="smallfont"> Quote:</div> <table border="0" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" width="99%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border-right: 1px inset; border-top: 1px inset; border-left: 1px inset; border-bottom: 1px inset">  Originally Posted by <strong>ReeRee</strong> <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/post/1371536"><img alt="View Post" border="0" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" /></a> <div style="font-style: italic"> You two look wonderful in those beautiful pics!! Question, where did your husband get his white shirts and slacks from?? I want my FI to have similar all white attire as well.</div> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div> Hey ReeRee,<br /> The shirt was Banana Republic and the pants were from Tristan (Canadian company). We saw similar ones at Armani Exchange.<br /> <br /> It&#39;s funny because his mom was so upset he was not going to be wearing a suit. She called us every day leading up to the wedding to get him to change his mind. After a while, he started shopping for blazers to appease her and I had to remind him that this original outfit is what he wanted. He looked great PLUS he would have been miserable with more clothes on in that heat.</blockquote> <p> <br /> Thank you Sunandsand! It gives me great idea where to shop for my FI!&nbsp; And I understand how in-laws can be sometimes;)<br /> &nbsp;</p>
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
