array (
  'pid' => '1253858',
  'post' => '<p> <br /> Â </p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>**Kat**</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/thread/933/budget/310#post_1350536"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border: 0px solid;" /></a><br /> <br /> <div style="margin: 5px 20px 20px;"> <div class="smallfont" style="margin-bottom: 2px;"> Quote:</div> <table border="0" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" width="99%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border: 1px inset;">  Originally Posted by <strong>pineapplebride</strong> <a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/post/1345428"><img alt="View Post" border="0" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" /></a> <div style="font-style: italic;"> The $5000 is based on the cost of bringing a local photographer we like to Mexico with us, which is our plan B.<br /> Originally we had dreamed of having Elizabeth Medina or Nathaniel Thompson, however they are both over the budget for the amount of coverage we want.<br /> <br /> If we can find a photographer we love for under $5000 we would be ecstatic!! I\'m going to check out your photos tonight!! Thx!</div> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div> Nate is AWESOME! (I have a link to his pro pics in my siggy) and WITH travel was WELLLLLLLLLLLLLLLLLLL under $5000! He is young and a LOT OF fun! Everyone raved about him!!<br /> <br /> Here is his email - <a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="mailto:nate.broshot@gmail.com">nate.broshot@gmail.com</a><br /> He is redoing his website at the moment so I think it is down right now, but it is <a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="http://www.licensetostill.com">License to Still Blog</a><br /> <br /> He is the best choice I made for my wedding!</blockquote> <p> <br /> Thanks for the suggestion!! I looked at Nates photos and they are brilliant! You must be SO happy with your wedding photos!!!<br /> <br /> Â </p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>vlynnw</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/thread/933/budget/310#post_1358429"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border: 0px solid;" /></a><br /> <br /> Pineapple bride - I\'m considering switching photogs (not too happy with mine) I\'ve been in contact with Nate, and if you are interested maybe we could see about splitting his travel cost since we are getting married the same week at DT if you wanted to use him.</blockquote> <p> <br /> I\'m sorry I didn\'t see you post until today! I\'ve been deglecting this forum (and wedding planning for that matter) trying to soak up as much of the sunshine as possible!! Sharing the travel costs of a photog would have been an awesome plan!! Did you end up booking Nate??</p> <p> Â </p> <p> FI and I found an awesome local photographer we are going to take with us to Mexico. Originally I was afraid her prices would be way out of our budget, but she gave us a few little discounts here and there and is going to pay 50% of the travel costs herself!!</p> <p> We are very excited!</p> <p> Â </p> <p> Â </p> <p> As for paying for the wedding. We are going to put everything on VISA... so we can rack up the avion points.... and then pay it off every month. We have vowed to not go $0.01 in debt for this wedding!!</p>',
)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
> Time: 1395962205 / Thu, 27 Mar 2014 23:16:45 +0000
> URL: /admin/index.php?adsess=845f6c850772369311b67ecf8645904c&app=forums&module=forums&section=fix&st=158250
> <p> <br /> Â </p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>**Kat**</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/thread/933/budget/310#post_1350536"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border: 0px solid;" /></a><br /> <br /> <div style="margin: 5px 20px 20px;"> <div class="smallfont"> Quote:</div> <table border="0" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" width="99%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border: 1px inset;">  Originally Posted by <strong>pineapplebride</strong> <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/post/1345428"><img alt="View Post" border="0" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" /></a> <div style="font-style: italic;"> The $5000 is based on the cost of bringing a local photographer we like to Mexico with us, which is our plan B.<br /> Originally we had dreamed of having Elizabeth Medina or Nathaniel Thompson, however they are both over the budget for the amount of coverage we want.<br /> <br /> If we can find a photographer we love for under $5000 we would be ecstatic!! I'm going to check out your photos tonight!! Thx!</div> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div> Nate is AWESOME! (I have a link to his pro pics in my siggy) and WITH travel was WELLLLLLLLLLLLLLLLLLL under $5000! He is young and a LOT OF fun! Everyone raved about him!!<br /> <br /> Here is his email - <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="mailto:nate.broshot@gmail.com">nate.broshot@gmail.com</a><br /> He is redoing his website at the moment so I think it is down right now, but it is <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="http://www.licensetostill.com">License to Still Blog</a><br /> <br /> He is the best choice I made for my wedding!</blockquote> <p> <br /> Thanks for the suggestion!! I looked at Nates photos and they are brilliant! You must be SO happy with your wedding photos!!!<br /> <br /> Â </p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>vlynnw</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/thread/933/budget/310#post_1358429"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border: 0px solid;" /></a><br /> <br /> Pineapple bride - I'm considering switching photogs (not too happy with mine) I've been in contact with Nate, and if you are interested maybe we could see about splitting his travel cost since we are getting married the same week at DT if you wanted to use him.</blockquote> <p> <br /> I'm sorry I didn't see you post until today! I've been deglecting this forum (and wedding planning for that matter) trying to soak up as much of the sunshine as possible!! Sharing the travel costs of a photog would have been an awesome plan!! Did you end up booking Nate??</p> <p> Â </p> <p> FI and I found an awesome local photographer we are going to take with us to Mexico. Originally I was afraid her prices would be way out of our budget, but she gave us a few little discounts here and there and is going to pay 50% of the travel costs herself!!</p> <p> We are very excited!</p> <p> Â </p> <p> Â </p> <p> As for paying for the wedding. We are going to put everything on VISA... so we can rack up the avion points.... and then pay it off every month. We have vowed to not go $0.01 in debt for this wedding!!</p>
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
