array (
  'pid' => '1281478',
  'post' => '<p> <br /> <br /> Â </p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>Boo</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/thread/29238/fernando-for-hair#post_1319772"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border-right: 0px solid; border-top: 0px solid; border-left: 0px solid; border-bottom: 0px solid" /></a><br /> <br /> I just booked a trial with Fernando. I am kinda nurveous though, maybe ladies who have already used him can comment - I would really appreciate that for my sanity, as my hair that day is very imporant.<br /> <br /> Hi, for those ladies who have gotten married already, I just sent a deposit, only to find after the fact that when Fernando said that he has no other weddings that day that I misunderstood and infact, he has already booked another one some time ago.<br /> <br /> Now my ceremony is at 2 pm, the other lady is on this forum and her ceremony is at 3:30. Mine is at Secrets Maroma and hers is at The Royal, PDC. We are both freaking out, I called him and he had indicated that this Saturday he has 3 and that this is typical. I just donâ€™t know what to do, I thought I would splurge as hair is super important to me and now I am worried its going to be a rush job for multiple of what I would have paid else where.<br /> <br /> Yikes this is just too stressful.<br /> <br /> Thanks for all your input.</blockquote> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>angelov321</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/thread/29238/fernando-for-hair#post_1319814"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border-right: 0px solid; border-top: 0px solid; border-left: 0px solid; border-bottom: 0px solid" /></a><br /> <br /> <div style="margin: 5px 20px 20px"> <div class="smallfont" style="margin-bottom: 2px"> Quote:</div> <table border="0" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" width="99%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border-right: 1px inset; border-top: 1px inset; border-left: 1px inset; border-bottom: 1px inset">  Originally Posted by <strong>Boo</strong> <a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/post/1319772"><img alt="View Post" border="0" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" /></a> <div style="font-style: italic"> I just booked a trial with Fernando. I am kinda nurveous though, maybe ladies who have already used him can comment - I would really appreciate that for my sanity, as my hair that day is very imporant.<br /> <br /> Hi, for those ladies who have gotten married already, I just sent a deposit, only to find after the fact that when Fernando said that he has no other weddings that day that I misunderstood and infact, he has already booked another one some time ago.<br /> <br /> Now my ceremony is at 2 pm, the other lady is on this forum and her ceremony is at 3:30. Mine is at Secrets Maroma and hers is at The Royal, PDC. We are both freaking out, I called him and he had indicated that this Saturday he has 3 and that this is typical. I just donâ€™t know what to do, I thought I would splurge as hair is super important to me and now I am worried its going to be a rush job for multiple of what I would have paid else where.<br /> <br /> Yikes this is just too stressful.<br /> <br /> Thanks for all your input.</div> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div> I just spoke to Fernando the other day and I had the same issue. Fernando felt really bad for having another wedding to attend to so he recommended his teacher to do my make-up instead. He assured me I wont be disappointed. Im scheduling a trial for the day before so I could have professional make-up and hair done for my welcome party. If it doesnt work out, then I will be out $150 and will just use the resorts salon for hair and make up.</blockquote> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>Mrs.S2B</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/thread/29238/fernando-for-hair/10#post_1382685"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border-right: 0px solid; border-top: 0px solid; border-left: 0px solid; border-bottom: 0px solid" /></a><br /> <br /> <p> Is this Fernando Fuentes in Playa del Carmen?? I did a make-up trial run with him and he brought someone with him to do my hair.&nbsp; Both did a great job and they are booked for my wedding in November.&nbsp; I hope all goes well since I am REALLY bad at doing my own make-up, even worse at doing my own hair!!!&nbsp; <img alt="" src="http://files.bestdestinationwedding.com/images/smilies/smile43.gif" title="" /></p> </blockquote> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>JYD1</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/thread/29238/fernando-for-hair/10#post_1424101"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border-right: 0px solid; border-top: 0px solid; border-left: 0px solid; border-bottom: 0px solid" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <p> <br /> Hi! I\'m considering using Fernando Fuents in Playa del Carmen as well. Do you have any pics from the trial? What was his fee that he quoted? Thanks!!<br /> Â </p> </blockquote> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>TLGnhci</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/thread/29238/fernando-for-hair/10#post_1424108"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border-right: 0px solid; border-top: 0px solid; border-left: 0px solid; border-bottom: 0px solid" /></a><br /> <br /> <p> I\'m interested&nbsp;in the pricing as well.&nbsp; And pics if you have them.&nbsp; Did you go to him, or did he come to your resort?&nbsp;</p> </blockquote> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>Boo</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/thread/29238/fernando-for-hair/10#post_1425585"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border-right: 0px solid; border-top: 0px solid; border-left: 0px solid; border-bottom: 0px solid" /></a><br /> <br /> <p> <span style="font-family: arial"><span style="color: black"><span style="font-size: 10pt">Fernando Fuentes </span></span></span></p> <p> Â </p> <p> <span style="font-family: arial"><span style="color: black"><span style="font-size: 10pt">his email&nbsp;</span></span></span><span style="font-family: arial"><span style="color: black"><span style="font-size: 10pt"><a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="javascript:noop()"><span style="color: #0000ff">&lt;themakeuppros@hotmail.com&gt;</span></a></span></span></span></p> <p> <span style="font-family: arial"><span style="color: black"><span style="font-size: 10pt">website </span></span></span><span style="font-family: arial"><span style="font-size: 10pt"><a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="http://www.the-makeup-pros.com/"><span style="color: #0000ff">www.the-makeup-pros.com </span></a></span></span></p> <p> Â </p> <p> <span style="font-family: arial"><span style="font-size: 10pt">BRIDE TRIAL HAIR AND MAKEUP $180<br /> DAY OF THE EVENT $350<br /> &nbsp;<br /> BRIDESMAIDS AND FAM<br /> ONLY MAKEUP $90<br /> ONLY HAIR $50 up to $80</span></span></p> </blockquote> <p> <br /> Please be aware of where you\'re posting this information - you\'re in the PV forum and are talking about a different stylist.<br /> Â </p>',
)
