> Time: 1395962205 / Thu, 27 Mar 2014 23:16:45 +0000
> URL: /admin/index.php?adsess=845f6c850772369311b67ecf8645904c&app=forums&module=forums&section=fix&st=158250
> 
array (
  'pid' => '1284007',
  'post' => '<p> Hi Kerrij,</p> <p> Â </p> <p> when did you find out about the final cost of your wedding and how did it work with the payment? Did you pay anything upfront except for the deposit/the wedding package you chose?</p> <p> How did you estimate the cost of your wedding. My fiance and I are having a hard time to get in touch with Beverly and we are so clueless about how to calculate how much we will be spending in the end. I hope you can help us.</p> <p> Â </p> <p> Thanks<br /> Â </p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>kerrij</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/thread/51518/any-gran-bahia-principe-runaway-bay-brides-out-there/120#post_1340556"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border: 0px solid;" /></a><br /> <br /> WOW!! there are so many GBP brides now!! Sorry i\'ve been MIA for a while...but i do check back and try to help answer questions...i know it\'s hard when you don\'t know what to expect and no one who\'s been married there is around to answer...so i try to come back often!!<br /> So excited for you girls! i want to come to all of your weddings!!! heck, i wanna move there! lol<br /> <br /> <br /> <div style="margin: 5px 20px 20px;"> <div class="smallfont" style="margin-bottom: 2px;"> Quote:</div> <table border="0" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" width="99%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border: 1px inset;">  Originally Posted by <strong>StephAli</strong> <a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/post/1296949"><img alt="View Post" border="0" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" /></a> <div style="font-style: italic;"> Hi Mekanabr,<br /> <br /> I decided on the sunshine package b/c its not much different then the blissful and is cheaper. I went through a travel agent to book everything and what we did was increase the price by $35per person so that it helps cover the additional plates...after all the flights are paid for the travel agent will refund me the "extra" money and I will bring that with me to the resort and give that money to Beverly....or put it on my credit card....I also confirmed that the date I wanted was available first, b/c I knew we wanted the specific date. Once she said that it was available I told the travel agent(s) what resort I wanted and then waited for them to get back to me...then I went with the best price!<br /> Hope this helps!<br /> Good Luck with the move!!!! <img alt="" border="0" class="inlineimg" src="http://files.bestdestinationwedding.com/images/smilies/cheesy.gif" title="Cheesy" /></div> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div> Hmmm...I\'m not sure if charging your guests an extra $35 is wrong/sneaky or if it\'s absolutely BRILLIANT!?! hahah i kinda wish i had thought of that because you don\'t really get any wedding gifts yet you still have to pay for all the guests meals, which im sure 99% of them don\'t even know that we pay out of our pocket for them still. but i prob would have felt bad doing it...unless i told them all that that extra charge was goign on there.<br /> <br /> <div style="margin: 5px 20px 20px;"> <div class="smallfont" style="margin-bottom: 2px;"> Quote:</div> <table border="0" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" width="99%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border: 1px inset;">  Originally Posted by <strong>jennypenny23</strong> <a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/post/1297189"><img alt="View Post" border="0" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" /></a> <div style="font-style: italic;"> StephAli- What is your ceremony date?? I have Feb 1st @ 3 pm booked with Beverly<br /> <br /> The thing that I am wondering about now (and maybe kerrij, you can clarify) is the thing about the "Gold Club" bracelets... I have a friend who went to this resort last year and she was saying that there are WAY more benefits if you upgrade to "gold"... I heard that you are then guaranteed the ala carte reservations, get the room safe for free, and room service?? I don\'t know if there is anything else or even if it is worth upgrading... We are planning on asking TA about this...<br /> <br /> Also- we really hope we get to stay in a really nice room!! Did any other GBP Jamaica brides have room upgrades? And how did you go about securing or \'requesting\' them<img alt="" border="0" class="inlineimg" src="http://files.bestdestinationwedding.com/images/smilies/huh.gif" title="Huh" /></div> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div> I read after this post that someone said absolutely upgrade....i fully DISAGREE!! soooo not worth the extra money! (IMO i\'ve always been a penny pincher too though) Bride/Groom get upgraded to Gold upon arrival, or after meeting Beverly...but we didn\'t even get use of our package, so i\'m gald we didn\'t apy for it. yes you get an extra dinner reservation and you get your dinners prebooked BUT we didn\'t go to any of them...we always joined in with other people from our group. or we hit up the awesome buffet. the room isn\'t an upgrade other than up higher and ocean view, but you can get that anyway if you just ask. all rooms have ocean view, some are just partial though. the room themselves apparently are all the same, no suites or anyting which i was sooooo disappointed with. the one thing i did like was room service...which we used once. it\'s a super limited menu...was nice to have the option though but not worth $120/person or wahtever it was, i\'d rather put that money towards first class which was the same price, and that\'s what we did for our flights! and the lounge thing was just free internet in a room...who wants the real wordl when you are in JAMAICA!! hahah aaahhhh!!!<br /> <br /> oh and your own area of the resort for gold members??!! never saw that or heard about it...no idea where it would be. but you\'ll want to be with your guests anyway!<br /> <br /> <div style="margin: 5px 20px 20px;"> <div class="smallfont" style="margin-bottom: 2px;"> Quote:</div> <table border="0" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" width="99%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border: 1px inset;">  Originally Posted by <strong>jennypenny23</strong> <a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/post/1316280"><img alt="View Post" border="0" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" /></a> <div style="font-style: italic;"> I am so excited about how many GBP Runaway bay Bride-to-be\'s there are now!!! Looking forward to sharing plans with everyone over the next couple of mths!! Our group rate is secured until June 16th so we will have our full guest list by then!! woohoo!!</div> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div> Congrats!!!<br /> <br /> <div style="margin: 5px 20px 20px;"> <div class="smallfont" style="margin-bottom: 2px;"> Quote:</div> <table border="0" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" width="99%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border: 1px inset;">  Originally Posted by <strong>sunchick31</strong> <a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/post/1318756"><img alt="View Post" border="0" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" /></a> <div style="font-style: italic;"> So I\'ve just returned from our wedding at GBP and this place is absolutely amazing! I am so sad that it\'s over because I would go back and do it again in a heartbeat! Beverly, the WC, is amazing and an absolute sweetheart! She took care of everything for us! The day couldn\'t have been more perfect and it\'s all thanks to her! We had a beautiful, sunny day and she was there with us every step of the way. We had our supper at the Grill Restaurant &amp; the food was delicious! Everyone loved it! We also decided on the reception in the Gazebo where we got married and I would highly recommend that! It is definitely worth it! We brought all of our own music and had the place rockin\'! All of our guests said it was the best wedding they have ever attended. I will recommend bringing your own photographer if possible. We didn\'t do that but luckily we had a few friends with professional cameras. I would have been rather upset if we didn\'t as the resort photographer didn\'t show up until the ceremony was over and then he only spent maybe a half hour with us! Luckily we also had a friend with a video camera who captured all our special moments. This resort is absolutely beautiful &amp; spotless! Our room was overlooking the pool &amp; the ocean as were most of our wedding guests\' rooms. We couldn\'t have gotten better treatment! All in all, I would recommend this resort to anyone who is looking for a place to get married! I was so sad to leave it &amp; cannot wait to return for our anniversary. Good Luck to all you future GBP brides! You are in for a treat!</div> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div> <br /> Hi Congrats!!!!!!!!!!!! soooo excitign for you!!! wasn\'t it just the BEST!!! i loved our wedding too!!!!!!<br /> And YES the disco music was awful! people even still say how bad it was!<br /> we took our own ipod and had a play list and plugged it into the DJs system.</blockquote> <br /> <br />',
)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
> Time: 1395962205 / Thu, 27 Mar 2014 23:16:45 +0000
> URL: /admin/index.php?adsess=845f6c850772369311b67ecf8645904c&app=forums&module=forums&section=fix&st=158250
