array (
  'pid' => '1288195',
  'post' => '<p> I finally CAVED and dove into this thread. Then Morgan\'s first post had me on a mission and I looked at all the top 1000 names from 2009, 1999 and 89. Yikes. So forgive my old MQ\'s but I had to. I\'m only on page 16... loving this thread though this far!!<br /> Â </p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>Debs</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/thread/47605/how-did-you-pick-your-baby-s-name/40#post_930882"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border: 0px solid;" /></a><br /> <br /> <div style="margin:20px; margin-top:5px; "> <div class="smallfont" style="margin-bottom:2px"> Quote:</div> <table border="0" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" width="99%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border:1px inset">  Originally Posted by <strong>Janet</strong> <a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/post/930756"><img alt="View Post" border="0" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" /></a> <div style="font-style:italic"> I LOVE LOVE the Baby Name Wizard,</div> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div> Ok, for a sec I thought you know the name you love is Wizard. And was wondering how many of you drank Morgan\'s Koolaid today!<br /> <br /> I also love the name Jared :)</blockquote> <p> <br /> I thought the same thing about Wizard Janet. LOL&nbsp;</p> <p> Â </p> <p> Jared I\'m quite fond of it too and I haven\'t seen ANY little Jared\'s lately. I guess it\'s not popular anymore.<br /> <br /> Â </p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>Debs</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/thread/47605/how-did-you-pick-your-baby-s-name/60#post_931498"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border: 0px solid;" /></a><br /> Debbie.<br /> <br /> <br /> My actual birth certificate name is Deborah. I hated my name when I was younger because it was unique. I was the only one in my whole school with that name. I remember crying to my dad that I hated it (Debbie). So he sat with me and said well your name is actually Deborah on your birth certificate, so Debbie can be spelled however you want. We went through all the different ways you could spell Debbie. I thought it was cool after that, and for all of grade 7 I was Debi. I have reports and school stuff with it spelled like that. Sometimes with a heart over the i.<br /> <br /> Now, it\'s more like strangers or people I don\'t know well call me Debbie. But good friends call me Deb. When C says Debbie I look at him strange.</blockquote> <p> <br /> <br /> My mom\'s name is Deborah goes by Debbie. My MIL is Debra too goes by Deb. hell breaks loose if you call her Debbie. Hah!&nbsp;<br /> Â </p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>ErinB</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/thread/47605/how-did-you-pick-your-baby-s-name/80#post_931693"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border: 0px solid;" /></a><br /> <br /> I have named all of my imaginary children! They are all girls, of course. God help me if I have a boy.<br /> <br /> I love older names and male names for girls.<br /> <br /> For years I\'ve said I would have:<br /> <br /> Lorelei Vincent<br /> Lorelei is really pretty and unique. It\'s German so that would reflect both of our lineage. Vincent is Mike\'s middle name.<br /> <br /> Lilian May<br /> My grandfather\'s mother was Lily and I am the only girl in generations whose middle name isn\'t May. Mom, G-ma, GG-ma, etc.<br /> <br /> Madeline Reese<br /> I have this thing for French culture and loved the Madeline books when I was a kid. I just love the name Reese.<br /> <br /> Cecila Grace<br /> No reasoning here. I just think it\'s pretty. Although, my Cabbage Patch\'s name was Darcie Cecile and I am a Simon &amp; Garfunkle fan so maybe it\'s subconscious...<br /> <br /> Wendell Wallace<br /> Wendell was my grandpa and Wallace is my dad and his dad\'s middle name.<br /> <br /> As a bonus, all of the names sound cool when you say them with an accent, LOL.<br /> <br /> Recently, as we have started talking about TTC, I\'m loving Harper, Piper, Edie (my grandma), Jolie (French for pretty), Annabelle (but that is too close to Isabell the dog), Elliot, and Hadley.<br /> Â </blockquote> <p> <br /> <br /> All you girl names are so beautiful! I\'m excited now that you\'re TTC Erin that one of these pretty names may be a possibility!<br /> Â </p> <br /> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>ErinB</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/thread/47605/how-did-you-pick-your-baby-s-name/90#post_931861"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border: 0px solid;" /></a><br /> <br /> Yeah, and there is a very real possibility that we could have red headed babies! maybe that isn\'t such a good name afterall, LOL</blockquote> <p> <br /> Us too! But I have kind of an olive complexion so it could be a scary thought. When Jared grows out his beard (gross hate it thank god for air force rules) it\'s all red. He hates on it so naturally I pick at him for it. Then we worry if we have kids and they end up with red hair and olive skin.&nbsp;<br /> <br /> Â </p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>Lizz</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/thread/47605/how-did-you-pick-your-baby-s-name/110#post_932410"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border: 0px solid;" /></a><br /> <br /> I love the name Aubrey for a girl. I think Aubrey Augelli would sound good. But I still think we\'re going with Ella if we have a girl next.<br /> <br /> I also love Irish names but they don\'t go so well with my new Italian last name. I love Declan, Seamus, Kieran, Patrick, Ryan, Donavan and plenty more but Mike nixed all of them<img alt="" border="0" class="inlineimg" src="http://files.bestdestinationwedding.com/images/smilies/sad.gif" title="Sad" /> If only I was still a Moran...lol!</blockquote> <p> <br /> Aubrey is one of my favorites!!!! BUT Jared said no to that one. All my names I adore he says no. Super picky that boy!<br /> <br /> Â </p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>starchild</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/thread/47605/how-did-you-pick-your-baby-s-name/130#post_937486"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border: 0px solid;" /></a><br /> <br /> I\'m loving the names you guys are sharing, fun! I\'m a biatch so I still refuse to share my lists but so far I\'ve only heard one name we\'ve talked about so that\'s encouraging. Plus, I\'m very not pregnant so I have time lol</blockquote> <p> <br /> So.... I have to ask. Was Lorenzo the name Jamy?!!</p> <p> Â </p> <p> We haven\'t dared to talk about middle names we can barely agree on first names but these are contenders:</p> <p> Â </p> <p> girl:</p> <p> Roslynn&nbsp;</p> <p> Kendall</p> <p> Kennedy</p> <p> Â </p> <p> boy:</p> <p> Tyson</p> <p> Brayden</p> <p> Â </p> <p> Jared has issues with so many names it\'s really hard to decide. He even looks at the intials as a deciding factor. LOL Plus we\'re not preggo. I keep saying the poor child will probably be nameless until he or she arrives. I\'m not inlove with any but Roslynn to be honest.&nbsp;</p> <p> Â </p> <p> Oh and having the last name Green is TOUGH! We both loved Hunter but that\'s a no no and there was a couple other ones where the color thing came into play. OK going back to read :0)</p>',
)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
