sound cool when you say them with an accent, LOL.<br /> <br /> Recently, as we have started talking about TTC, I'm loving Harper, Piper, Edie (my grandma), Jolie (French for pretty), Annabelle (but that is too close to Isabell the dog), Elliot, and Hadley.<br /> Â </blockquote> <p> <br /> <br /> All you girl names are so beautiful! I'm excited now that you're TTC Erin that one of these pretty names may be a possibility!<br /> Â </p> <br /> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>ErinB</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/thread/47605/how-did-you-pick-your-baby-s-name/90#post_931861"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border: 0px solid;" /></a><br /> <br /> Yeah, and there is a very real possibility that we could have red headed babies! maybe that isn't such a good name afterall, LOL</blockquote> <p> <br /> Us too! But I have kind of an olive complexion so it could be a scary thought. When Jared grows out his beard (gross hate it thank god for air force rules) it's all red. He hates on it so naturally I pick at him for it. Then we worry if we have kids and they end up with red hair and olive skin.&nbsp;<br /> <br /> Â </p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>Lizz</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/thread/47605/how-did-you-pick-your-baby-s-name/110#post_932410"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border: 0px solid;" /></a><br /> <br /> I love the name Aubrey for a girl. I think Aubrey Augelli would sound good. But I still think we're going with Ella if we have a girl next.<br /> <br /> I also love Irish names but they don't go so well with my new Italian last name. I love Declan, Seamus, Kieran, Patrick, Ryan, Donavan and plenty more but Mike nixed all of them<img alt="" border="0" class="inlineimg" src="http://files.bestdestinationwedding.com/images/smilies/sad.gif" title="Sad" /> If only I was still a Moran...lol!</blockquote> <p> <br /> Aubrey is one of my favorites!!!! BUT Jared said no to that one. All my names I adore he says no. Super picky that boy!<br /> <br /> Â </p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>starchild</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/thread/47605/how-did-you-pick-your-baby-s-name/130#post_937486"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border: 0px solid;" /></a><br /> <br /> I'm loving the names you guys are sharing, fun! I'm a biatch so I still refuse to share my lists but so far I've only heard one name we've talked about so that's encouraging. Plus, I'm very not pregnant so I have time lol</blockquote> <p> <br /> So.... I have to ask. Was Lorenzo the name Jamy?!!</p> <p> Â </p> <p> We haven't dared to talk about middle names we can barely agree on first names but these are contenders:</p> <p> Â </p> <p> girl:</p> <p> Roslynn&nbsp;</p> <p> Kendall</p> <p> Kennedy</p> <p> Â </p> <p> boy:</p> <p> Tyson</p> <p> Brayden</p> <p> Â </p> <p> Jared has issues with so many names it's really hard to decide. He even looks at the intials as a deciding factor. LOL Plus we're not preggo. I keep saying the poor child will probably be nameless until he or she arrives. I'm not inlove with any but Roslynn to be honest.&nbsp;</p> <p> Â </p> <p> Oh and having the last name Green is TOUGH! We both loved Hunter but that's a no no and there was a couple other ones where the color thing came into play. OK going back to read :0)</p>
