> Time: 1395962206 / Thu, 27 Mar 2014 23:16:46 +0000
> URL: /admin/index.php?adsess=845f6c850772369311b67ecf8645904c&app=forums&module=forums&section=fix&st=158250
> 
array (
  'pid' => '1309738',
  'post' => '<p> <br /> &nbsp;</p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>lauren</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/thread/60573/pf-what-s-on-your-bucket-list/10#post_1337374"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border-bottom: 0px solid; border-left: 0px solid; border-top: 0px solid; border-right: 0px solid" /></a><br /> <br /> <div style="margin: 5px 20px 20px"> <div class="smallfont" style="margin-bottom: 2px"> Quote:</div> <table border="0" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" width="99%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border-bottom: 1px inset; border-left: 1px inset; border-top: 1px inset; border-right: 1px inset">  Originally Posted by <strong>-Kate-</strong> <a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/post/1336276"><img alt="View Post" border="0" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" /></a> <div style="font-style: italic"> I have the 101 in 1001 list to so some of my stuff is on there. The one I\'m working on now from my bucket list is donate hair to locks of love. You have to have 10 inches to donate so lets hope I can hang in there and not get it chopped before then.</div> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div> <font color="darkorange">would donating to pantene suffice? you only need 8 inches for that. i\'ve given to LOL twice, and pantene once...pantene was a less traumatizing haircut....</font><br /> <br /> <div style="margin: 5px 20px 20px"> <div class="smallfont" style="margin-bottom: 2px"> &nbsp;</div> <div class="smallfont" style="margin-bottom: 2px"> &nbsp;</div> <div class="smallfont" style="margin-bottom: 2px"> &nbsp;</blockquote> </div> </div> I was going to ask the same thing. If you can\'t make 10 inches, you at least have this option. The pantene program makes wigs for cancer patients. Locks of love is mostly allopecia, but they only work with kids. Pantene is adults, too. I donated my grown-out-for-the-wedding hair last year. It was rough towards the end because it was a tabgled mess. but, I loved my short haircut. Now I am tired of the every 7 week hair appointments, so I\'m letting it grow. I was just thinking how I need to make a real list & write it down. I usually just know it when it pops in my head, but I can\'t name whats on the list. Doing a grape stomp was on my list & I just checked that off. Puking on a table after a grape stomp was not on the list. Lately, the only things on my mental bucket list are places to shoot or a mental image of a photo I want to take. I tease my mom that her bucket list adapts to whatever activity she wants us to include her in. I was planning a rafting trip with friends & she announced it was on her bucket list so she came with us. Same for the hawaii trip. Oh, I thought of another. Riding a zipline. Off to work on the list...',
)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
> Time: 1395962206 / Thu, 27 Mar 2014 23:16:46 +0000
> URL: /admin/index.php?adsess=845f6c850772369311b67ecf8645904c&app=forums&module=forums&section=fix&st=158250
> <p> <br /> &nbsp;</p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>lauren</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/thread/60573/pf-what-s-on-your-bucket-list/10#post_1337374"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border-bottom: 0px solid; border-left: 0px solid; border-top: 0px solid; border-right: 0px solid" /></a><br /> <br /> <div style="margin: 5px 20px 20px"> <div class="smallfont"> Quote:</div> <table border="0" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" width="99%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border-bottom: 1px inset; border-left: 1px inset; border-top: 1px inset; border-right: 1px inset">  Originally Posted by <strong>-Kate-</strong> <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/post/1336276"><img alt="View Post" border="0" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" /></a> <div style="font-style: italic"> I have the 101 in 1001 list to so some of my stuff is on there. The one I'm working on now from my bucket list is donate hair to locks of love. You have to have 10 inches to donate so lets hope I can hang in there and not get it chopped before then.</div> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div> <font color="darkorange">would donating to pantene suffice? you only need 8 inches for that. i've given to LOL twice, and pantene once...pantene was a less traumatizing haircut....</font><br /> <br /> <div style="margin: 5px 20px 20px"> <div class="smallfont"> &nbsp;</div> <div class="smallfont"> &nbsp;</div> <div class="smallfont"> &nbsp;</blockquote> </div> </div> I was going to ask the same thing. If you can't make 10 inches, you at least have this option. The pantene program makes wigs for cancer patients. Locks of love is mostly allopecia, but they only work with kids. Pantene is adults, too. I donated my grown-out-for-the-wedding hair last year. It was rough towards the end because it was a tabgled mess. but, I loved my short haircut. Now I am tired of the every 7 week hair appointments, so I'm letting it grow. I was just thinking how I need to make a real list & write it down. I usually just know it when it pops in my head, but I can't name whats on the list. Doing a grape stomp was on my list & I just checked that off. Puking on a table after a grape stomp was not on the list. Lately, the only things on my mental bucket list are places to shoot or a mental image of a photo I want to take. I tease my mom that her bucket list adapts to whatever activity she wants us to include her in. I was planning a rafting trip with friends & she announced it was on her bucket list so she came with us. Same for the hawaii trip. Oh, I thought of another. Riding a zipline. Off to work on the list...
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
