> <p> This poem is great! Thanks for sharing!<br /> <br /> &nbsp;</p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>pryzeless</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/thread/21183/sign-on-guestbook-table/20#post_383570"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border-right: 0px solid; border-top: 0px solid; border-left: 0px solid; border-bottom: 0px solid" /></a><br /> <br /> <div style="margin: 5px 20px 20px"> <div class="smallfont"> Quote:</div> <table border="0" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" width="99%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border-right: 1px inset; border-top: 1px inset; border-left: 1px inset; border-bottom: 1px inset">  Originally Posted by <strong>BeckyN</strong> <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/post/383183"><img alt="View Post" border="0" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" /></a> <div style="font-style: italic"> I'm still debating what I want to do for my guestbook... If I do a photomat or plate I will probably just assign someone to be in charge of it.<br /> <br /> If I go for the photobook type thing - where w/ the help of my ex-MOH I am going to make it a scrapbook with the photos of each group and their wish/advice written to us on squares of cardstock or something - I would probably set up a sign like the one below to explain what I want.<br /> <br /> <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="http://i82.photobucket.com/albums/j252/becky2ann/Planning%20Stuff/Ceremony%20Ideas/Guestbookquote.jpg"><img alt="Click the image to open in full size." border="0" class="tcattdimgresizer" src="http://i82.photobucket.com/albums/j252/becky2ann/Planning%20Stuff/Ceremony%20Ideas/Guestbookquote.jpg" /></a></div> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div> I love this. Thanks for sharing.</blockquote> <br /> <br />
