> <p> very professional-looking!<br /> &nbsp;</p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>MsShelley</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/thread/5868/tags-for-welcome-bags/10#post_134458"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border: 0px solid;" /></a><br /> <br /> <div style="margin:20px; margin-top:5px; "> <div class="smallfont"> Quote:</div> <table border="0" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" width="99%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border:1px inset">  Originally Posted by <strong>cheese_diva</strong> <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/post/134387"><img alt="View Post" border="0" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" /></a> <div style="font-style:italic"> I just made these tags for my welcome bags. I bought two different size hole punches (2.5" + 2") and punched cut scrapbook paper for the background, then printed our logo on white cardstock and glued to circle. I then cut another smaller white circle and will write the guests name on the back (rather than printing and having last minute changes, etc.)<br /> <br /> One more thing off my list!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="http://i148.photobucket.com/albums/s22/cheese_diva/misc/100_1302.jpg"><img alt="Click the image to open in full size." border="0" class="tcattdimgresizer" src="http://i148.photobucket.com/albums/s22/cheese_diva/misc/100_1302.jpg" /></a><br /> <br /> <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="http://i148.photobucket.com/albums/s22/cheese_diva/misc/100_1301.jpg"><img alt="Click the image to open in full size." border="0" class="tcattdimgresizer" src="http://i148.photobucket.com/albums/s22/cheese_diva/misc/100_1301.jpg" /></a></div> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div> OMG!! they are so cute!! I love them!</blockquote> <br /> <br /> <p> &nbsp;</p>
