> Time: 1395962206 / Thu, 27 Mar 2014 23:16:46 +0000
> URL: /admin/index.php?adsess=845f6c850772369311b67ecf8645904c&app=forums&module=forums&section=fix&st=158250
> 
array (
  'pid' => '1482241',
  'post' => '<p> i\'m going to comment based on my 6 months as a mom...<br /> &nbsp;</p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>AnnR</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/thread/48003/what-baby-stuff-do-you-really-need#post_943718"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border: 0px solid;" /></a><br /> <div style="margin: 5px 20px 20px;"> <table border="0" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" width="99%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border: 1px inset;"> &nbsp;</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div> Quote:<br /> <div style="margin: 5px 20px 20px;"> <table border="0" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" width="99%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border: 1px inset;">  Originally Posted by <strong>Lizz</strong> <a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/post/943650"><img alt="View Post" border="0" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" /></a> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <br /> <strong>car seat </strong>- <span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);"><strong>we have a graco snugride. just the plain one. the suggested height is 26 inches, which logan has surpassed, but the weight is 22lbs. it\'s getting heavy to carry him in it and i won\'t have to very much longer, as he\'s getting better at sitting. </strong></span></div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);"><strong>k has a recaro for his car. we haven\'t used it yet. i have to get a convertible for my car, but haven\'t looked into it yet.</strong></span><br /> <br /> <strong>stroller</strong> - <strong><span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);">we have the first years wave stroller. so far i love it. it comes w/ a universal attachment for the snugride, and the seat part doubles as a bassinette. it IS 2 pieces, but it\'s easy to put together and can be taken apart w/ one hand. </span></strong><br /> <br /> <strong>Kippopatamous swaddlers &amp; Halo sleep sacks</strong> - <strong><span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);">logan was swaddled until about 3 months. if he wasn\'t swaddled, he\'d wake himself up. he used sleep sacks for a bit after that, but i can see that totally being up to the baby. i\'d get some, wash one, and keep the receipts.</span></strong><br /> <br /> <br /> <strong>diapers</strong> - don\'t invest in tons of diapers til you see what you prefer; I had cases of Huggies and ended up only liking Pampers<br /> <br /> <font color="seagreen">i only ever tried Pampers Swaddlers and Huggies - didn\'t like Huggies as much.</font></div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> &nbsp;</div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <strong><span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);">HATED huggies. like pampers and am currently using target. i can see that target would be good for size 1-2, but logan needs more of a cruiser diaper than a swaddler and the target ones are a bit big for cruising.</span></strong><br /> <br /> <strong>bottles</strong> -<span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);"><strong> logan never did the boob, so i\'m glad i had bottles. i have 6 large and probably 10 small. i think i use about 5/day. i don\'t HAVE to wash them daily, but i do have to wash the nipples. we use born free. tried 2 others, but these worked best.</strong></span><br /> <br /> <strong>Baby Bjorn</strong> - I LOVE this and still use it now even though Drew is getting a little heavy for it. It\'s so easy to put him in when we\'re out at the store instead of carrying him or using a stroller.<br /> <br /> <font color="seagreen">i have a bjorn (hand-me-down), a babyhawk (mei tei) and a sling. never used the sling, and used the bjorn a lot for a period of time. i\'ve used the babyhawk a few times. this one (baby carriers) is really an individual mommy and baby choice!</font></div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> &nbsp;</div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <strong><span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);">i have a hand-me-down bjorn. i registered for an ergo, but logan HATED it. he is ok in the bjorn for short periods of time. i\'m short though, so he dangles past my hips!</span></strong><br /> <br /> <strong>Video monitor</strong> - We\'ve used this from day one. I love that I can see what he\'s doing even when I\'m down the basement or outside.<br /> <br /> <font color="seagreen">we just have a sound monitor and i never found the need for a video. this one has been discussed at length somewhere, so i won\'t do it again ... and i know that i am in the minority! i just never felt the urge to watch gwen sleep at all times. lol</font><br /> <br /> <font color="#2e8b57">at home gwen\'s bedroom is downstairs and ours is up so we need a monitor. now in the UK we don\'t need even a monitor - we can hear her well enough from anywehre in teh house.</font></div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> &nbsp;</div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);"><strong>we have an angel care monitor. idk what i would have done w/o it, especially when we couldn\'t regulate the temperature in the house. knowing that he\'s breathing gives me peace of mind. i don\'t need video, though it would be helpful sometimes when he\'s up and i want to see how much longer i have until he starts yelling at me to get up...</strong></span><br /> <br /> <strong>Swing/bouncy seat</strong> - We didn\'t use either that much but I bought them on CL so I don\'t regret the money I spent b/c they were used some. I bought the FP rocker chair too for $5 on CL and we use that all of the time now for him to eat in. I like that one best b/c it goes up to 35 lbs.<br /> <br /> <font color="seagreen">we didn\'t use the boucner much at all other than just somewhere to set her when we needed to put her down. early on she didn\'t like to be put down anywhere, so it didnt\' really matter. we actually had a FP papasan which didnt\' bounce but it did have a vibrate option. so i\'d call it her vibrator rather than her bouncer - paul hated that. </font><br /> <br /> <font color="#2e8b57">anyway, for a while gwen would only sleep in her swing so it was worth the money for me. but i could have just done with a used one off of CL or something.</font></div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> &nbsp;</div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);"><strong>we used the swing for the first 2 months if we were in the basement and he needed to nap. he never relied on it. should have gotten from CL but was a gift. definitely used the bouncy seat b/c i needed a place to put him when i was pumping. we still use it for that. </strong></span><br /> <br /> <strong>Jumperoo</strong> - Drew\'s favorite thing...love it!<br /> <br /> <font color="seagreen">this one i did get off of CL when i saw how much she loved it when we were at someone else\'s house. for a few months she loved it, even fell asleep while jumping! but once that phase was over it was just big and in the way.</font></div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> &nbsp;</div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);"><strong>logan loves it. </strong></span><br /> <br /> <strong>Play mat</strong> - We used this ALL of the time, highly recommend buying one.<br /> <br /> <font color="seagreen">definitely worth getting for us - especially since they don\'t cost much!</font></div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> &nbsp;</div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);"><strong>we use it all the time too b/c we don\'t have carpet anywhere but the basement. logan still likes to sit under the arches and grab the toys</strong></span><span style="font-weight: bold;">.</span><br /> <br /> <strong>Pack &amp; Play</strong> - We used this all of the time too. We have one with the changing table and we used it til he got too heavy for it. He took naps in the pack &amp; play til he was about 3 months old and now we use it when traveling.<strong><span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);">&lt;--- yes</span></strong>.<br /> <br /> <font color="seagreen">we didn\'t use ours too much until now - here in the UK it\'s her full time bed! but worth getting, especially if you and/or baby travel or just stay at friends/relatives houses. one with the bassinet feature is handy.</font></div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <br /> <br /> <strong>JJ Cole Bundle Me &amp; strap covers &amp; Kippopatamous snuzzler</strong> - We never used the bundle me, snuzzler or car seat strap covers. It seems like they were on a lot of people\'s registries so I added them to mine but we never had a use for them.<br /> <br /> ditto. we actually had 2 bundle mes - the heavier one and a lighter one. i tried them a few times but they just drove me nuts and got in the way. it was just as easy to throw a blanket over her. and technically if you ask a car seat specialist, you shouldn\'t use them. since they "interfere" with the car seats straps and buckles, they\'re not recomended. basically they say if it doesnt\' come with teh car seat or it cahnges how the car seat straps and harnesses are used, don\'t use them. your call - plenty of moms do!</div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> &nbsp;</div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <strong><span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);">i used the bundle me b/c logan was born in december. i never put a coat or snowsuit on him b/c i had the bundle me. didn\'t get strap covers, haven\'t needed them. used the head part of the snuzzler for a few weeks, but the body part + the bundle me = too much. i did just buy logan a neck support pillow for use in the car seat when we go on long drives.</span></strong><br /> <br /> <strong>Boppy</strong> - I used this for feeding and when he was learning to sit up. I liked it but could have done without.<br /> <br /> <font color="seagreen">i used mine all of the time. when feeding, and just to set her in so she was propped up - worked well since she had reflux i didn\'t want her laying back flat.</font></div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> &nbsp;</div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <strong><span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);">i could have done w/o. if logan took the boob, i could see how it would have been more useful.</span></strong><br /> <br /> <strong>Medicines etc.</strong> - Definitely get some gas drops, infant tylenol, nasal aspirator, thermometer, nail clippers, etc. We\'ve needed all of them.<br /> <br /> <font color="seagreen">ditto. </font></div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> &nbsp;</div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);"><strong>target gas drops, target tylenol, cheapo rectal thermometer, use the bulb aspirator from the hospital.</strong></span><br /> <br /> <strong>Baby bathtub</strong> - We\'ve used this from day one and still use it. I have the First Years newborn-to-toddler tub and it\'s great because now he\'s using the toddler part b/c he can sit up.<br /> <br /> <font color="seagreen">i used my tub all of the time as well. then she got too big and someone gave us (again, hand-me-down) a tub seat thing. she\'s big enough to be without, but she\'s so dang squirmy and goes nuts in the tub! i use the seat about 1/2 the time now - we bought on here in London.</font></div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> &nbsp;</div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);"><strong>we have the first years one too. we used it until logan could sit up supported. then we bathed in the bumbo. now we bathe in the kitchen sink. </strong></span><br /> <br /> <strong>Baby robes</strong> - We received 3 robes as gifts and have never used them. I tried to put one on Drew once and he hated it.<br /> <br /> <font color="seagreen">i never bothered with robes - a PITA in my opnion. i think she has like 2-3 of them. same with slippers.</font></div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> &nbsp;</div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <strong><span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);">never got any.</span></strong><br /> <br /> <strong>Hooded bath towels, washclothes, burpies</strong> - I use these all of the time<br /> <br /> <font color="seagreen">ditto. well, the hooded towels i could do w/o but i did use mine.</font></div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> &nbsp;</div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <strong><span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);">i like the hooded towels. we have 4 and i could use 1 more.</span></strong><br /> <br /> <strong>Receiving blankets</strong> - I have more of these than I can count and have never used them<br /> <br /> <font color="seagreen">gwen spit up a TON so i often used the blankets as large burp cloths. and also just to lay under her on teh floor or couch when i put her down. i carried them everywhere and was a must have for us! i had a ton and was always washing them - but again, mostly because of the excessive spit up.</font></div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> &nbsp;</div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);"><strong>barely used, and when i did they are used as burp cloths. i use cloth diapers as burp cloths. </strong></span><br /> <br /> <strong>Bottle cooler</strong> - only used once when we went to the beach<br /> <br /> <font color="seagreen">never had one. nuff said.</font></div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> &nbsp;</div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);"><strong>i have a bunch of insulated bottle holders but no coolers.</strong></span><br /> <br /> <strong>Bottle sterilizer, drying rack and brushes, dishwasher baskets</strong> - use these every day<br /> <br /> <font color="seagreen">never had any of this except a drying rack. still use the drying rack - for a lot more than bottles too.</font></div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> &nbsp;</div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);"><strong>no sterilizer. definitely use the rack, have gone through about 8 brushes, and use the basket b/c otherwise things would get lost in my dishwasher.</strong></span><br /> <br /> <strong>Sleep positioner</strong> - used this til he was about 4 months old<br /> <br /> <font color="seagreen">never had one. i did have a wedge that we used only because of her reflux. not sure it made a difference or not. we did put rolled up blankets at her side when we found she was rolling down the wedge at night though.</font></div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> &nbsp;</div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <strong><span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);">think these are off the market now. did use a rolled up blanket a few times when he was especially spit-uppy. </span></strong><br /> <br /> <strong>Bumpers</strong> - we have the bumpers that came with his room stuff but ended up taking them off and buying the Breathable Bumpers a few months ago and love them. <strong>&lt;--- yep.</strong><br /> <br /> <font color="seagreen">gwen has always had bumpers on her bed - i could go either way with these.</font><br /> <br /> <strong>Detergent</strong> - I bought Dreft a few times but now just buy Target brand free &amp; clear detergent and use it for all of our laundry...much easier and cheaper.<br /> <br /> <font color="seagreen">All free &amp; clear I think - just something w/o chemicals and dyes.</font></div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> &nbsp;</div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);"><strong>we started w/ kirkland free and clear, but everything smelled like crap, so we\'re back to the regular tide that we\'ve always used.</strong></span><br /> <br /> <strong>Bins/baskets</strong> - I have SO many of these and use them to store all of his stuff - toys, diapers, etc.<br /> <br /> <font color="seagreen">i did buy quite a few things to organize her room and the living room where we hang out.</font></div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> &nbsp;</div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <strong><span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);">have a few. anticipate buying a few more as he accumulates more toys.</span></strong><br /> <br /> <strong>Formula dispenser, infant bowls &amp; spoons, baby cubes food trays, bibs (both cloth &amp; vinyl)</strong> - use them all of the time<br /> <br /> <font color="seagreen">ditto - well, gwen never had formula but we used it for cereal.</font></div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> &nbsp;</div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <strong><span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);">bumkins (sp?) bibs are awesome. food wipes right off. currently use regular bowls that i found for $.98 at target, but will have to get some w/ bottom suction cups soon. </span></strong><br /> &nbsp;</div> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </blockquote> </div> <br /> <br /> <p> &nbsp;</p> <br /> <br /> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>AnnR</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/thread/48003/what-baby-stuff-do-you-really-need#post_943807"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border: 0px solid;" /></a><br /> <br /> Mo has a few more things on here, so I will add my comments ...<br /> <br /> <div style="margin: 5px 20px 20px;"> <div class="smallfont" style="margin-bottom: 2px;"> Quote:</div> <table border="0" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" width="99%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border: 1px inset;">  Originally Posted by <strong>TA Maureen</strong> <a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/post/943770"><img alt="View Post" border="0" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" /></a> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <br /> <br /> <strong>Wipes</strong>-Again we tried everything but like Pampers sensitive skin wipes the best.<br /> <br /> <font color="seagreen">this is what we use too - though i haven\'t tried too many other brands.</font></div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> &nbsp;</div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <strong>bought kirkland from costco. 900 wipes for $20.</strong><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <strong>The Numer One Most Useless Baby Item for us-The Diaper Champ</strong> no matter what kind of contraption you get the bottom line is you have to open it some time and when you do it is absoultuely foul. We only used it for pee diapers and it was still foul. Do not waste your money. We bring all pee pee diapers to the kitchen trash can which is in the closet and gets taken out every night. #2\'s get bagged in grocery store plastic bags which I keep handy and go directly outside to the garbage can. I don\'t care what the weather is like or how far away I am from the back door. There is no reason to stockpile shit diapers in your home to be removed at a later time!<br /> <br /> <font color="seagreen">pretty sure i am in the minority here too, but i wish i had my Diaper Genie here! (I think we actually have the II). we just have a regular ol\' garbage can w/a lid in gwen\'s room here and man does it stink up the room. i might even buy something here like the diaper genie (or diaper champ). we just don\'t go to the hassle of bringing her poopie diapers out every time, so i want somewhere close by to throw them. her room at home doesn\'t stink ... her room here does!</font></div> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </blockquote> </div> <p> we have a diaper genie (i think...) and it stinks to high holy hell. it\'s disgusting.</p> <p> &nbsp;</p> <p> i got <strong>diaper bags </strong>- amy coe, maybe vanilla scented? - and use those for especially stinky poos. i keep some in my diaper bag.<br /> &nbsp;</p> <p> we also have an <strong>exersaucer </strong>which is priceless. b/c my house is wood throughout, we need a place to put him down that is safe for him. i can put him on a blanket on the floor, but once he started rolling over, he started banging his head - the blanket was not enough to prevent him from hurting himself.</p> <p> &nbsp;</p> <p> we always use our <strong>changing table</strong> and our glider. idk what i\'d do w/o a <strong>good glider</strong>.</p>',
)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
> Time: 1395962206 / Thu, 27 Mar 2014 23:16:46 +0000
> URL: /admin/index.php?adsess=845f6c850772369311b67ecf8645904c&app=forums&module=forums&section=fix&st=158250
> <p> i'm going to comment based on my 6 months as a mom...<br /> &nbsp;</p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>AnnR</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/thread/48003/what-baby-stuff-do-you-really-need#post_943718"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border: 0px solid;" /></a><br /> <div style="margin: 5px 20px 20px;"> <table border="0" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" width="99%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border: 1px inset;"> &nbsp;</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div> Quote:<br /> <div style="margin: 5px 20px 20px;"> <table border="0" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" width="99%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border: 1px inset;">  Originally Posted by <strong>Lizz</strong> <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/post/943650"><img alt="View Post" border="0" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" /></a> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <br /> <strong>car seat </strong>- <span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);"><strong>we have a graco snugride. just the plain one. the suggested height is 26 inches, which logan has surpassed, but the weight is 22lbs. it's getting heavy to carry him in it and i won't have to very much longer, as he's getting better at sitting. </strong></span></div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);"><strong>k has a recaro for his car. we haven't used it yet. i have to get a convertible for my car, but haven't looked into it yet.</strong></span><br /> <br /> <strong>stroller</strong> - <strong><span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);">we have the first years wave stroller. so far i love it. it comes w/ a universal attachment for the snugride, and the seat part doubles as a bassinette. it IS 2 pieces, but it's easy to put together and can be taken apart w/ one hand. </span></strong><br /> <br /> <strong>Kippopatamous swaddlers &amp; Halo sleep sacks</strong> - <strong><span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);">logan was swaddled until about 3 months. if he wasn't swaddled, he'd wake himself up. he used sleep sacks for a bit after that, but i can see that totally being up to the baby. i'd get some, wash one, and keep the receipts.</span></strong><br /> <br /> <br /> <strong>diapers</strong> - don't invest in tons of diapers til you see what you prefer; I had cases of Huggies and ended up only liking Pampers<br /> <br /> <font color="seagreen">i only ever tried Pampers Swaddlers and Huggies - didn't like Huggies as much.</font></div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> &nbsp;</div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <strong><span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);">HATED huggies. like pampers and am currently using target. i can see that target would be good for size 1-2, but logan needs more of a cruiser diaper than a swaddler and the target ones are a bit big for cruising.</span></strong><br /> <br /> <strong>bottles</strong> -<span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);"><strong> logan never did the boob, so i'm glad i had bottles. i have 6 large and probably 10 small. i think i use about 5/day. i don't HAVE to wash them daily, but i do have to wash the nipples. we use born free. tried 2 others, but these worked best.</strong></span><br /> <br /> <strong>Baby Bjorn</strong> - I LOVE this and still use it now even though Drew is getting a little heavy for it. It's so easy to put him in when we're out at the store instead of carrying him or using a stroller.<br /> <br /> <font color="seagreen">i have a bjorn (hand-me-down), a babyhawk (mei tei) and a sling. never used the sling, and used the bjorn a lot for a period of time. i've used the babyhawk a few times. this one (baby carriers) is really an individual mommy and baby choice!</font></div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> &nbsp;</div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <strong><span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);">i have a hand-me-down bjorn. i registered for an ergo, but logan HATED it. he is ok in the bjorn for short periods of time. i'm short though, so he dangles past my hips!</span></strong><br /> <br /> <strong>Video monitor</strong> - We've used this from day one. I love that I can see what he's doing even when I'm down the basement or outside.<br /> <br /> <font color="seagreen">we just have a sound monitor and i never found the need for a video. this one has been discussed at length somewhere, so i won't do it again ... and i know that i am in the minority! i just never felt the urge to watch gwen sleep at all times. lol</font><br /> <br /> <font color="#2e8b57">at home gwen's bedroom is downstairs and ours is up so we need a monitor. now in the UK we don't need even a monitor - we can hear her well enough from anywehre in teh house.</font></div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> &nbsp;</div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);"><strong>we have an angel care monitor. idk what i would have done w/o it, especially when we couldn't regulate the temperature in the house. knowing that he's breathing gives me peace of mind. i don't need video, though it would be helpful sometimes when he's up and i want to see how much longer i have until he starts yelling at me to get up...</strong></span><br /> <br /> <strong>Swing/bouncy seat</strong> - We didn't use either that much but I bought them on CL so I don't regret the money I spent b/c they were used some. I bought the FP rocker chair too for $5 on CL and we use that all of the time now for him to eat in. I like that one best b/c it goes up to 35 lbs.<br /> <br /> <font color="seagreen">we didn't use the boucner much at all other than just somewhere to set her when we needed to put her down. early on she didn't like to be put down anywhere, so it didnt' really matter. we actually had a FP papasan which didnt' bounce but it did have a vibrate option. so i'd call it her vibrator rather than her bouncer - paul hated that. </font><br /> <br /> <font color="#2e8b57">anyway, for a while gwen would only sleep in her swing so it was worth the money for me. but i could have just done with a used one off of CL or something.</font></div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> &nbsp;</div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);"><strong>we used the swing for the first 2 months if we were in the basement and he needed to nap. he never relied on it. should have gotten from CL but was a gift. definitely used the bouncy seat b/c i needed a place to put him when i was pumping. we still use it for that. </strong></span><br /> <br /> <strong>Jumperoo</strong> - Drew's favorite thing...love it!<br /> <br /> <font color="seagreen">this one i did get off of CL when i saw how much she loved it when we were at someone else's house. for a few months she loved it, even fell asleep while jumping! but once that phase was over it was just big and in the way.</font></div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> &nbsp;</div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);"><strong>logan loves it. </strong></span><br /> <br /> <strong>Play mat</strong> - We used this ALL of the time, highly recommend buying one.<br /> <br /> <font color="seagreen">definitely worth getting for us - especially since they don't cost much!</font></div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> &nbsp;</div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);"><strong>we use it all the time too b/c we don't have carpet anywhere but the basement. logan still likes to sit under the arches and grab the toys</strong></span><span style="font-weight: bold;">.</span><br /> <br /> <strong>Pack &amp; Play</strong> - We used this all of the time too. We have one with the changing table and we used it til he got too heavy for it. He took naps in the pack &amp; play til he was about 3 months old and now we use it when traveling.<strong><span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);">&lt;--- yes</span></strong>.<br /> <br /> <font color="seagreen">we didn't use ours too much until now - here in the UK it's her full time bed! but worth getting, especially if you and/or baby travel or just stay at friends/relatives houses. one with the bassinet feature is handy.</font></div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <br /> <br /> <strong>JJ Cole Bundle Me &amp; strap covers &amp; Kippopatamous snuzzler</strong> - We never used the bundle me, snuzzler or car seat strap covers. It seems like they were on a lot of people's registries so I added them to mine but we never had a use for them.<br /> <br /> ditto. we actually had 2 bundle mes - the heavier one and a lighter one. i tried them a few times but they just drove me nuts and got in the way. it was just as easy to throw a blanket over her. and technically if you ask a car seat specialist, you shouldn't use them. since they "interfere" with the car seats straps and buckles, they're not recomended. basically they say if it doesnt' come with teh car seat or it cahnges how the car seat straps and harnesses are used, don't use them. your call - plenty of moms do!</div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> &nbsp;</div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <strong><span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);">i used the bundle me b/c logan was born in december. i never put a coat or snowsuit on him b/c i had the bundle me. didn't get strap covers, haven't needed them. used the head part of the snuzzler for a few weeks, but the body part + the bundle me = too much. i did just buy logan a neck support pillow for use in the car seat when we go on long drives.</span></strong><br /> <br /> <strong>Boppy</strong> - I used this for feeding and when he was learning to sit up. I liked it but could have done without.<br /> <br /> <font color="seagreen">i used mine all of the time. when feeding, and just to set her in so she was propped up - worked well since she had reflux i didn't want her laying back flat.</font></div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> &nbsp;</div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <strong><span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);">i could have done w/o. if logan took the boob, i could see how it would have been more useful.</span></strong><br /> <br /> <strong>Medicines etc.</strong> - Definitely get some gas drops, infant tylenol, nasal aspirator, thermometer, nail clippers, etc. We've needed all of them.<br /> <br /> <font color="seagreen">ditto. </font></div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> &nbsp;</div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);"><strong>target gas drops, target tylenol, cheapo rectal thermometer, use the bulb aspirator from the hospital.</strong></span><br /> <br /> <strong>Baby bathtub</strong> - We've used this from day one and still use it. I have the First Years newborn-to-toddler tub and it's great because now he's using the toddler part b/c he can sit up.<br /> <br /> <font color="seagreen">i used my tub all of the time as well. then she got too big and someone gave us (again, hand-me-down) a tub seat thing. she's big enough to be without, but she's so dang squirmy and goes nuts in the tub! i use the seat about 1/2 the time now - we bought on here in London.</font></div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> &nbsp;</div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);"><strong>we have the first years one too. we used it until logan could sit up supported. then we bathed in the bumbo. now we bathe in the kitchen sink. </strong></span><br /> <br /> <strong>Baby robes</strong> - We received 3 robes as gifts and have never used them. I tried to put one on Drew once and he hated it.<br /> <br /> <font color="seagreen">i never bothered with robes - a PITA in my opnion. i think she has like 2-3 of them. same with slippers.</font></div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> &nbsp;</div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <strong><span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);">never got any.</span></strong><br /> <br /> <strong>Hooded bath towels, washclothes, burpies</strong> - I use these all of the time<br /> <br /> <font color="seagreen">ditto. well, the hooded towels i could do w/o but i did use mine.</font></div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> &nbsp;</div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <strong><span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);">i like the hooded towels. we have 4 and i could use 1 more.</span></strong><br /> <br /> <strong>Receiving blankets</strong> - I have more of these than I can count and have never used them<br /> <br /> <font color="seagreen">gwen spit up a TON so i often used the blankets as large burp cloths. and also just to lay under her on teh floor or couch when i put her down. i carried them everywhere and was a must have for us! i had a ton and was always washing them - but again, mostly because of the excessive spit up.</font></div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> &nbsp;</div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);"><strong>barely used, and when i did they are used as burp cloths. i use cloth diapers as burp cloths. </strong></span><br /> <br /> <strong>Bottle cooler</strong> - only used once when we went to the beach<br /> <br /> <font color="seagreen">never had one. nuff said.</font></div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> &nbsp;</div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);"><strong>i have a bunch of insulated bottle holders but no coolers.</strong></span><br /> <br /> <strong>Bottle sterilizer, drying rack and brushes, dishwasher baskets</strong> - use these every day<br /> <br /> <font color="seagreen">never had any of this except a drying rack. still use the drying rack - for a lot more than bottles too.</font></div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> &nbsp;</div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);"><strong>no sterilizer. definitely use the rack, have gone through about 8 brushes, and use the basket b/c otherwise things would get lost in my dishwasher.</strong></span><br /> <br /> <strong>Sleep positioner</strong> - used this til he was about 4 months old<br /> <br /> <font color="seagreen">never had one. i did have a wedge that we used only because of her reflux. not sure it made a difference or not. we did put rolled up blankets at her side when we found she was rolling down the wedge at night though.</font></div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> &nbsp;</div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <strong><span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);">think these are off the market now. did use a rolled up blanket a few times when he was especially spit-uppy. </span></strong><br /> <br /> <strong>Bumpers</strong> - we have the bumpers that came with his room stuff but ended up taking them off and buying the Breathable Bumpers a few months ago and love them. <strong>&lt;--- yep.</strong><br /> <br /> <font color="seagreen">gwen has always had bumpers on her bed - i could go either way with these.</font><br /> <br /> <strong>Detergent</strong> - I bought Dreft a few times but now just buy Target brand free &amp; clear detergent and use it for all of our laundry...much easier and cheaper.<br /> <br /> <font color="seagreen">All free &amp; clear I think - just something w/o chemicals and dyes.</font></div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> &nbsp;</div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);"><strong>we started w/ kirkland free and clear, but everything smelled like crap, so we're back to the regular tide that we've always used.</strong></span><br /> <br /> <strong>Bins/baskets</strong> - I have SO many of these and use them to store all of his stuff - toys, diapers, etc.<br /> <br /> <font color="seagreen">i did buy quite a few things to organize her room and the living room where we hang out.</font></div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> &nbsp;</div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <strong><span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);">have a few. anticipate buying a few more as he accumulates more toys.</span></strong><br /> <br /> <strong>Formula dispenser, infant bowls &amp; spoons, baby cubes food trays, bibs (both cloth &amp; vinyl)</strong> - use them all of the time<br /> <br /> <font color="seagreen">ditto - well, gwen never had formula but we used it for cereal.</font></div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> &nbsp;</div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <strong><span style="color: rgb(255, 140, 0);">bumkins (sp?) bibs are awesome. food wipes right off. currently use regular bowls that i found for $.98 at target, but will have to get some w/ bottom suction cups soon. </span></strong><br /> &nbsp;</div> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </blockquote> </div> <br /> <br /> <p> &nbsp;</p> <br /> <br /> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>AnnR</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/thread/48003/what-baby-stuff-do-you-really-need#post_943807"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border: 0px solid;" /></a><br /> <br /> Mo has a few more things on here, so I will add my comments ...<br /> <br /> <div style="margin: 5px 20px 20px;"> <div class="smallfont"> Quote:</div> <table border="0" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" width="99%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border: 1px inset;">  Originally Posted by <strong>TA Maureen</strong> <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/post/943770"><img alt="View Post" border="0" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" /></a> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <br /> <br /> <strong>Wipes</strong>-Again we tried everything but like Pampers sensitive skin wipes the best.<br /> <br /> <font color="seagreen">this is what we use too - though i haven't tried too many other brands.</font></div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> &nbsp;</div> <div style="font-style: italic;"> <strong>bought kirkland from costco. 900 wipes for $20.</strong><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <strong>The Numer One Most Useless Baby Item for us-The Diaper Champ</strong> no matter what kind of contraption you get the bottom line is you have to open it some time and when you do it is absoultuely foul. We only used it for pee diapers and it was still foul. Do not waste your money. We bring all pee pee diapers to the kitchen trash can which is in the closet and gets taken out every night. #2's get bagged in grocery store plastic bags which I keep handy and go directly outside to the garbage can. I don't care what the weather is like or how far away I am from the back door. There is no reason to stockpile shit diapers in your home to be removed at a later time!<br /> <br /> <font color="seagreen">pretty sure i am in the minority here too, but i wish i had my Diaper Genie here! (I think we actually have the II). we just have a regular ol' garbage can w/a lid in gwen's room here and man does it stink up the room. i might even buy something here like the diaper genie (or diaper champ). we just don't go to the hassle of bringing her poopie diapers out every time, so i want somewhere close by to throw them. her room at home doesn't stink ... her room here does!</font></div> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </blockquote> </div> <p> we have a diaper genie (i think...) and it stinks to high holy hell. it's disgusting.</p> <p> &nbsp;</p> <p> i got <strong>diaper bags </strong>- amy coe, maybe vanilla scented? - and use those for especially stinky poos. i keep some in my diaper bag.<br /> &nbsp;</p> <p> we also have an <strong>exersaucer </strong>which is priceless. b/c my house is wood throughout, we need a place to put him down that is safe for him. i can put him on a blanket on the floor, but once he started rolling over, he started banging his head - the blanket was not enough to prevent him from hurting himself.</p> <p> &nbsp;</p> <p> we always use our <strong>changing table</strong> and our glider. idk what i'd do w/o a <strong>good glider</strong>.</p>
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
