array (
  'pid' => '1501887',
  'post' => '<p> <br /> <br /> thanks for the website.</p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>RaychelRae</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/thread/18087/show-off-your-shoes/610#post_1228480"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border-bottom: 0px solid; border-left: 0px solid; border-top: 0px solid; border-right: 0px solid" /></a><br /> <br /> <div style="margin: 5px 20px 20px"> <div class="smallfont" style="margin-bottom: 2px"> Quote:</div> <table border="0" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" width="99%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border-bottom: 1px inset; border-left: 1px inset; border-top: 1px inset; border-right: 1px inset">  Originally Posted by <strong>LadyTrunck</strong> <a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/post/1228172"><img alt="View Post" border="0" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" /></a> <div style="font-style: italic"> So how do you plan on doing the \'blinging\'? Just curious, because I may have to do it on a pair of my shoes!!! I\'ve been able to copy some stuff with DIY, but figuring that one out seems a little daunting. The only thing I\'ve blinged, was a pimp cup for a bachelorette party! haha. But I used a glue gun, and that would not work for shoes.</div> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div> I found this website called Crystals2Love and they have everything you need to rhinestone something. They sell individual swarovski crystals in all sizes and colors plus the specific kind of glue you need and these little sticks with wax on the end of them to pick up each little crystal and place it on whatever you\'re crystaling. They aren\'t bad priced either. If I end up liking my shoes I ordered, I\'m going to start crystaling them right away b/c it will pry take me a year to finish them! Well worth it though! ; )</blockquote> <br /> <br /> <p> &nbsp;</p>',
)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
> Time: 1395962206 / Thu, 27 Mar 2014 23:16:46 +0000
> URL: /admin/index.php?adsess=845f6c850772369311b67ecf8645904c&app=forums&module=forums&section=fix&st=158250
> <p> <br /> <br /> thanks for the website.</p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>RaychelRae</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/thread/18087/show-off-your-shoes/610#post_1228480"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border-bottom: 0px solid; border-left: 0px solid; border-top: 0px solid; border-right: 0px solid" /></a><br /> <br /> <div style="margin: 5px 20px 20px"> <div class="smallfont"> Quote:</div> <table border="0" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" width="99%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border-bottom: 1px inset; border-left: 1px inset; border-top: 1px inset; border-right: 1px inset">  Originally Posted by <strong>LadyTrunck</strong> <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/post/1228172"><img alt="View Post" border="0" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" /></a> <div style="font-style: italic"> So how do you plan on doing the 'blinging'? Just curious, because I may have to do it on a pair of my shoes!!! I've been able to copy some stuff with DIY, but figuring that one out seems a little daunting. The only thing I've blinged, was a pimp cup for a bachelorette party! haha. But I used a glue gun, and that would not work for shoes.</div> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div> I found this website called Crystals2Love and they have everything you need to rhinestone something. They sell individual swarovski crystals in all sizes and colors plus the specific kind of glue you need and these little sticks with wax on the end of them to pick up each little crystal and place it on whatever you're crystaling. They aren't bad priced either. If I end up liking my shoes I ordered, I'm going to start crystaling them right away b/c it will pry take me a year to finish them! Well worth it though! ; )</blockquote> <br /> <br /> <p> &nbsp;</p>
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
