array (
  'pid' => '1510244',
  'post' => '<p> This information is SOOO helpful!!&nbsp; Thanks for sharing.&nbsp; I am doing this!&nbsp; :)<br /> &nbsp;</p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>JUSTUSTWO</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/t/35759/my-oot-bags-the-big-hits-and-the-things-that-weren-t-used/10#post_669339"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border: 0px solid;" /></a><br /> <br /> <div style="margin: 5px 20px 20px;"> <div class="smallfont" style="margin-bottom: 2px;"> Quote:</div> <table border="0" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" width="99%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border: 1px inset;">  Originally Posted by <strong>Anthony\'sGirl</strong> <a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/post/669271"><img alt="View Post" border="0" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" /></a> <div style="font-style: italic;"> I found a bunch of travel mugs at the dollar store and was thinking of just getting waterproof paper and printing our monogram and sticking them on there? Anyone else done this? Good/bad idea??</div> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div> A few BDW brides have bought travel cups &amp; then personalized them with waterproof labels &amp; markers.<br /> They came out really cute. I would do a few as tests to see how well they hold up before you buy them in large quantities.<br /> <br /> Here\'s a thread that I found that may give you some ideas:<br /> <a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="http://bestdestinationwedding.com/forum/t33350">http://bestdestinationwedding.com/forum/t33350</a><br /> <br /> I knew someone on here had done this before so I went looking for the thread &amp; found it.<br /> This thread has the pics of the mugs:<br /> <a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="http://bestdestinationwedding.com/forum/t13580">http://bestdestinationwedding.com/forum/t13580</a><br /> <br /> And this one tells how she did it &amp; what materials she used:<br /> <a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="http://bestdestinationwedding.com/forum/t13574">http://bestdestinationwedding.com/forum/t13574</a><br /> <br /> Morgan did these as well. Take a look at her planning thread:<br /> <a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="http://bestdestinationwedding.com/forum/t21764">http://bestdestinationwedding.com/forum/t21764</a></blockquote> <br /> <br /> <p> &nbsp;</p>',
)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
> Time: 1395962207 / Thu, 27 Mar 2014 23:16:47 +0000
> URL: /admin/index.php?adsess=845f6c850772369311b67ecf8645904c&app=forums&module=forums&section=fix&st=158250
> <p> This information is SOOO helpful!!&nbsp; Thanks for sharing.&nbsp; I am doing this!&nbsp; :)<br /> &nbsp;</p> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>JUSTUSTWO</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/t/35759/my-oot-bags-the-big-hits-and-the-things-that-weren-t-used/10#post_669339"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" style="border: 0px solid;" /></a><br /> <br /> <div style="margin: 5px 20px 20px;"> <div class="smallfont"> Quote:</div> <table border="0" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" width="99%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border: 1px inset;">  Originally Posted by <strong>Anthony'sGirl</strong> <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/post/669271"><img alt="View Post" border="0" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" /></a> <div style="font-style: italic;"> I found a bunch of travel mugs at the dollar store and was thinking of just getting waterproof paper and printing our monogram and sticking them on there? Anyone else done this? Good/bad idea??</div> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div> A few BDW brides have bought travel cups &amp; then personalized them with waterproof labels &amp; markers.<br /> They came out really cute. I would do a few as tests to see how well they hold up before you buy them in large quantities.<br /> <br /> Here's a thread that I found that may give you some ideas:<br /> <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="http://bestdestinationwedding.com/forum/t33350">http://bestdestinationwedding.com/forum/t33350</a><br /> <br /> I knew someone on here had done this before so I went looking for the thread &amp; found it.<br /> This thread has the pics of the mugs:<br /> <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="http://bestdestinationwedding.com/forum/t13580">http://bestdestinationwedding.com/forum/t13580</a><br /> <br /> And this one tells how she did it &amp; what materials she used:<br /> <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="http://bestdestinationwedding.com/forum/t13574">http://bestdestinationwedding.com/forum/t13574</a><br /> <br /> Morgan did these as well. Take a look at her planning thread:<br /> <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="http://bestdestinationwedding.com/forum/t21764">http://bestdestinationwedding.com/forum/t21764</a></blockquote> <br /> <br /> <p> &nbsp;</p>
