array (
  'pid' => '1714624',
  'post' => '<blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>KRama</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/t/786/gran-bahia-principe-akumal-tulum-coba-post-here/2950#post_1313981"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" /></a><br /> <br /> <div style="margin: 5px 20px 20px;"> <div class="smallfont" style="margin-bottom: 2px;"> Quote:</div> <table border="0" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" width="99%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border: 1px inset currentColor;">  Originally Posted by <strong>jjohnson30</strong> <a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="/forum/post/1313731"><img alt="View Post" border="0" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" /></a> <div style="font-style: italic;"> hi, my&nbsp;</div> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div> Hi Jessica, I hope this helps you out! Here\'s some pics from my wedding that was 3 weeks ago (gasp! 3 weeks already!). We got married at Coba but I imagine the table set ups would be similar.<br /> <br /> Head table:<br /> <a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="http://i937.photobucket.com/albums/ad215/Krama/Fulltable-1.jpg"><img alt="Click the image to open in full size." border="0" class="tcattdimgresizer" src="http://i937.photobucket.com/albums/ad215/Krama/Fulltable-1.jpg" /></a><br /> <br /> The head table had the flower arrangement from the ceremony. The rest had small vases with a single flower and little candle lanterns. When we arrived, they had large silver platters with a customized menu at each place setting. I brought down the table cards with my guests names, that was it!<br /> <br /> <a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="http://i937.photobucket.com/albums/ad215/Krama/TableSetting.jpg"><img alt="Click the image to open in full size." border="0" class="tcattdimgresizer" src="http://i937.photobucket.com/albums/ad215/Krama/TableSetting.jpg" /></a><br /> <br /> This was the cake we had:<br /> <br /> <a data-ipb=\'nomediaparse\' href="http://i937.photobucket.com/albums/ad215/Krama/Cake.jpg"><img alt="Click the image to open in full size." border="0" class="tcattdimgresizer" src="http://i937.photobucket.com/albums/ad215/Krama/Cake.jpg" /></a><br /> <br /> We had 40 people attend but we didn\'t bother to upgrade the cake since we were serving dessert with dinner. We chose the chocolate cake and it was delicious! I think this is the standard size/shape/look of the cake that\'s included in the package so if you want something different I suggest emailing your WC with pics and get her to provide you with the cost.<br /> <br /> Hope that helps! If you have any other questions, ask away!<br /> <br /> Oh and I promise to get to that review this weekend!!</blockquote> <p> If you stay in COBA do you have to eat at the resturants there, or can you choose from any of the options?&nbsp; and what kind of food was at the Portfinio?</p> <p> Did you have to pay extra because you had more then 30 guests?&nbsp; Did you do your speachs there or somewhere else?&nbsp; and Did you have the dances in the resturant or outside after dinner? Are there other dinners in there with you while your having your reception or is it just your Group?</p>',
)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
> Time: 1395962207 / Thu, 27 Mar 2014 23:16:47 +0000
> URL: /admin/index.php?adsess=845f6c850772369311b67ecf8645904c&app=forums&module=forums&section=fix&st=158250
> <blockquote class="ipsBlockquote">Originally Posted by <strong>KRama</strong>&nbsp;<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/t/786/gran-bahia-principe-akumal-tulum-coba-post-here/2950#post_1313981"><img alt="View Post" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" /></a><br /> <br /> <div style="margin: 5px 20px 20px;"> <div class="smallfont"> Quote:</div> <table border="0" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" width="99%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="alt2" style="border: 1px inset currentColor;">  Originally Posted by <strong>jjohnson30</strong> <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="/forum/post/1313731"><img alt="View Post" border="0" class="inlineimg" src="/img/forum/go_quote.gif" /></a> <div style="font-style: italic;"> hi, my&nbsp;</div> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div> Hi Jessica, I hope this helps you out! Here's some pics from my wedding that was 3 weeks ago (gasp! 3 weeks already!). We got married at Coba but I imagine the table set ups would be similar.<br /> <br /> Head table:<br /> <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="http://i937.photobucket.com/albums/ad215/Krama/Fulltable-1.jpg"><img alt="Click the image to open in full size." border="0" class="tcattdimgresizer" src="http://i937.photobucket.com/albums/ad215/Krama/Fulltable-1.jpg" /></a><br /> <br /> The head table had the flower arrangement from the ceremony. The rest had small vases with a single flower and little candle lanterns. When we arrived, they had large silver platters with a customized menu at each place setting. I brought down the table cards with my guests names, that was it!<br /> <br /> <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="http://i937.photobucket.com/albums/ad215/Krama/TableSetting.jpg"><img alt="Click the image to open in full size." border="0" class="tcattdimgresizer" src="http://i937.photobucket.com/albums/ad215/Krama/TableSetting.jpg" /></a><br /> <br /> This was the cake we had:<br /> <br /> <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href="http://i937.photobucket.com/albums/ad215/Krama/Cake.jpg"><img alt="Click the image to open in full size." border="0" class="tcattdimgresizer" src="http://i937.photobucket.com/albums/ad215/Krama/Cake.jpg" /></a><br /> <br /> We had 40 people attend but we didn't bother to upgrade the cake since we were serving dessert with dinner. We chose the chocolate cake and it was delicious! I think this is the standard size/shape/look of the cake that's included in the package so if you want something different I suggest emailing your WC with pics and get her to provide you with the cost.<br /> <br /> Hope that helps! If you have any other questions, ask away!<br /> <br /> Oh and I promise to get to that review this weekend!!</blockquote> <p> If you stay in COBA do you have to eat at the resturants there, or can you choose from any of the options?&nbsp; and what kind of food was at the Portfinio?</p> <p> Did you have to pay extra because you had more then 30 guests?&nbsp; Did you do your speachs there or somewhere else?&nbsp; and Did you have the dances in the resturant or outside after dinner? Are there other dinners in there with you while your having your reception or is it just your Group?</p>
